dustrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T07:59:42-08:00","id":400317,"title":"","content":"We should just get a Lunar Core for the forum.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lun-Lunars, Lunars Lunars, wanna go to Lunars, Lunars Lunars, Dad are you in Lunars? Yes son, now we are all a Lunars family again. Lunars Lunars L-L-L-Lunars.<br /> <br /> &quot;LUNNNNAAARRRRSSSSSSS. LLLLUUUNNNNNANAAAARRRRRRRRSSSSS. Bopbopbopbobpbopbpbopb wanna go to Lunars. YES SPELL IT ELL You Ehn LUNARS.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-size:9px\">...getting bored of Lunars....&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:36:51-08:00","id":400371,"title":"","content":"I've always been curious, in an effort to salvage a thread. I know we harp on constantly about how terrible and shit Lunars of 1e are, but I propose a challenge. What from Lunars 1e can actually be salvaged, or better yet isn't actually that bad or bad at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:39:16-08:00","id":400398,"title":"","content":"I'm glad someone did it. I would have just been mean about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400290#post400290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget, we're leaving Lunars out of Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh, if only...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:49:53-08:00","id":400410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400371#post400371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been curious, in an effort to salvage a thread. I know we harp on constantly about how terrible and shit Lunars of 1e are, but I propose a challenge. What from Lunars 1e can actually be salvaged, or better yet isn't actually that bad or bad at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even 2e Lunars could be salvaged, with a lot of work. Or get the right people to crunch it and just revamp the whole thing; I think I even saw someone redo the lost castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T09:14:33-08:00","id":400435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400410#post400410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even 2e Lunars could be salvaged, with a lot of work. Or get the right people to crunch it and just revamp the whole thing; I think I even saw someone redo the lost castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep they don't need to be torn down entirely and built again, the fact is that despite their issues the Lunars have become iconic and beloved to Exalted fans, even their flaws can be loved sometimes. I think my approach to &quot;fixing&quot; Lunars wouldn't be changing them from what they were in 1e and 2e. I would leave them the same but give them extra tools to be new things as well, and write new canon examples of those tools being used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T09:16:59-08:00","id":400437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400371#post400371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What from Lunars 1e can actually be salvaged, or better yet isn't actually that bad or bad at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmm. Ummmmm....<br /> <br /> I like Tammuz and shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T11:36:05-08:00","id":400585,"title":"","content":"Just a little (and hopefully unnecessary) reminder to keep things respectful, it's one thing to mock the Lunar topics but steer clear of personal or group attacks.<br /> Thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:24:13-08:00","id":400679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If our Anima banners are iconic to our &quot;soul&quot;, I always found it silly to limit it to our Spirit Shape.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't actually mind the animal stuff. Just pointing out a few quibbles, extrapolating by the text <i>forcing us</i> to stick to our furry critter. Sometimes my No Moons envy the Twilights and Midnights and such who can just pick abstract or occult symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was happier once I realized that a Lunar's icon only had to reference their spirit shape, not mimic it exactly.<br /> <br /> I could have the image of a giant cat, or a more abstracted symbol in which, upon close inspection, one can see the Cheshire's grin, as with BlazBlue's Taokaka's iconic display.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More specifically, with many canon Exalts inheriting their symbols from their previous incarnations (ie, this is a hero <i>reborn</i>, and the Exaltation seeks like heros), it makes it kind of weird (because at some point, someone would notice &quot;yeah, we've had the same 3 Octopus totem Lunars, 5 Spiders, 24 Wolves, 32 Cats and (after reaching all 300) oh shit, our Lunars completely ignore 99% of the animal kingdom because we're all replaying the same old tropes over and over. </div> </div> </div>I don't see the worth in getting bent out of shape regarding the shapes that people choose, whether players or characters.<br /> <br /> No one ever said the Lunar Exalted Host has to fairly represent the diversity of the animal kingdom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or equally bad - no one recognizes my anima, because unlike the Solars, my legend isn't eternal in any sense. <i>No one</i> will look upon my anima with hope and go &quot;my long dead wife, reborn&quot; or gaze upon it with dread and realize their enemy is reborn. </div> </div> </div>Why not? Why wouldn't this be so?<br /> <br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of this to say,<b> I liked Chimera as done in 1st Edition </b>because at least I could grow as a character (and change) and have my allegedly &quot;Spirit&quot; shape reflect those changes (I've never had an interest in forming a Garou tribe and serving as a template for some beastmen). Earning the disrespect of other Lunars (while not being auto-killed as a potential monster) was also nice. </div> </div> </div>I'm already considering a character who mixed the totems of Tiger and Bull, resulting in the Square Enix studio's interpretation of the Behemoth... but also a bestial representation of the Japanese <i>oni</i>, a demon said to have the claws and fangs of a tiger and the horns of the bull*. The fact that this is very similar to Western visions of devils is a neat bonus of inspiration as well.<br /> <br /> *The entrance to the demon world was believed to be in the North-West, between the directions associated with the astrological signs of Tiger and Ox. So naturally, the Japanese envisioned the quintessential demon as a mix between those two beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:40:30-08:00","id":400702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/392812-handling-the-forum-engsmplosion?p=393093#post393093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a stunning last-second change, the entire Sail Ability has been removed and replaced with the Lunar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/392812-handling-the-forum-engsmplosion/page2?_=1423600647905\">actual quote</a> and I will be holding Vance to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:07:47-08:00","id":400830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there were some 1st Age Swan-totem Lunar ambassadors - who after the Usurpation and bloodshed and suffering - would ditch the Swan and return as a glorious Lion</div> </div> </div> </div> But then you miss out on beating people to death with your wings!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:13:08-08:00","id":400835,"title":"","content":"I thought the default was getting a new totemic anima banner when you exalt, with only a few people keeping it from the first age. In fact your totem can change during your lifetime if a big event happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:13:53-08:00","id":400837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400585#post400585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a little (and hopefully unnecessary) reminder to keep things respectful, it's one thing to mock the Lunar topics but steer clear of personal or group attacks.<br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it alright if I mock my own tendency to cooonstantly repost my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost\">Lunar Exaltation Homebrew Fluff</a> at any possible chance?<br /> <br /> Or my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/196987-celestial-bonds-old-forum-repost\">Celestial Bonds</a>? Can't forget that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:22:14-08:00","id":400840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Panther flares up - the 1st Age Heirophant had the same banner. If Swan goes Totemic - Desus also had the same anima banner. Even with Abyssals and Infernals, some seem to acquire &quot;deathly&quot; or &quot;demonic&quot; renditions of their old selves (and I might be misremembering, but I thought one of them explicitly saw images of 1st Age atrocities they committed in their new banner, sustaining the link between identities even as the symbol changed). Etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mehhhhhhh. Meh meh meh. This can go <i>as a default</i>. Whoever decided to write this kind of thing as a normative baseline was trying way too hard to impose their view of the game onto all tables of it, and lucky for them they got a platform to do so as a writer, and that's really a problem because of how it stifles choices. <br /> <br /> If a player says &quot;my PC is named Swan, and here's his anima banner that I came up with, and A Cool Thing is that it's actually the same anima banner as his prior incarnation from the First Age, Desus, whom everyone thought was a cool guy but he was really a master manipulator and sociopath&quot; that's cool, that's a tie that the player has innovated which can have story effects.<br /> <br /> It's also a <i>deliberate choice</i>. Which is always better than &quot;hey, Ryan, you said you're playing a diplomat/martial artist named Swan, right? And you came up with his prior incarnation, Desus, as a story point that Swan doesn't really know about right? Well you have the same anima banner as this asshole wife-beater named Desus. Hope you don't flare around any god that might remember what a douchebag 'you' were 3000 years ago! Hyuk hyuk!&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel the same way about the 2e notion of how Celestial Exaltations generally picked the same kind of people consistently, like if Zenith Exaltation #7 really liked to pick young, assertive shrine maidens so most of its incarnations fit this mould, including the current player. It makes the whole thing way too wooden and mechanical for me, and less interesting than <i>the player </i>discovering that their character's prior incarnation was entirely like them--or entirely unlike them--through the natural course of plot.<br /> <br /> It's quite different if such a thing is spelled out to players right in the books as a thing they have to intentionally subvert or it's assumed they conform to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:42:21-08:00","id":400907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I]I found this happiness as well, although I'm pretty sure I avoid some Spirit Shape options entirely because of their Anima and Tell effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, the Tell will go back to its First Edition variability, where it didn't have to be a bestial feature. Like Beast Boy's green coloration.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let crippling deformities be Tells, though, unless such a thing specifically prevented the Lunar from ever recovering from that deformity. The devs have said they've found a way to introduce Flaws into the game in a way they like, and I could see a Lunar take a Flaw as a Tell as easily as a physical &quot;mutation&quot; Merit.<br /> <br /> On which note, I want to be able to make a &quot;mutation&quot; into my Tell. I want to be able to choose a bull's horns, and always have the bull's horns in all of my forms (assuming that's what Tells still do), but almost no one can actually notice my horns without a really good Awareness.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: And by &quot;mutation/Merit&quot;, I mean I want my Tell to be functionally weaponized horns that I can use to gore someone, even if they couldn't see my horns until their blood is coating them.)<br /> <br /> Which also reminds me, I want a sensible explanation as to why my Lunar Essence is trying to reveal my nature through a Tell while simultaneously trying to hide the Tell it is revealing. That's like someone forcing me to wear a shirt that says &quot;Kick Me&quot;, but then also forcing me to put on a jacket to hide the shirt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My go-to default has usually been Octopus. Instead of hentacles, I go off the Ink they produce. A creepy Tell - a shifting shadow resembling an Octopus ink blot. A similarly dark and vague Anima banner (and just like an Octopus, I'm deep inside the display of whirls and such). Plenty of people mistook her Tell for an Abyssal with Resonance bleed. </div> </div> </div>That's cool.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, if you wanted to make her a Chimera, you could cross in snakes -- or electric eels, or moray eels -- so that each of her tentacles headed in an independent snapping head! Sort of like <i>Ranma 1/2</i>'s idea of the Orochi, with a single large head (in this case, the octopus) from which all the other necks and smaller heads extended.<br /> <br /> Going even further with Chimerism might make each tentacle-head different; one with crushing jaws (moray eel), electric jaws (electric eel), venomous jaws, fire breath, keen senses (because the heads improve your environmental awareness as well as attack options)...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was just an idle thought in the sense of &quot;if one of these Lunar moot things really happened, I can't be the only one who notices 1/3 of our entire Host is composed of 10 or so species. </div> </div> </div>Genre-blindness. When superheroes get together, few of them ever mention how many of them are orphans. Or supermodels who choose to wear spandex.<br /> <br /> Or white, male and heterosexual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;equally bad&quot; was the implied <i>opposite - instead of </i>&quot;all Lunars throughout history will be the same 300 totems, repeated forever and ever&quot;, it was &quot;your Totem has no connection to your previous lives, so no one will associate my 2nd Age Octopus totem with my 1st Age Anglerfish totem&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Lunars <i>do</i> change Castes between incarnations more frequently than other Exalted (by virtue of being the ONLY Exalted who can do so, rather than because of how often it does or doesn't actually happen), but Lunars are not supposed to change icons any more frequently than Solars.<br /> <br /> With Celestial Exalted, whether you have the same iconic banner as your previous incarnation has always been a matter of player choice, just like &quot;how much of his past life does my character even <i>remember</i>?&quot; Or, for that matter, how many <i>other people </i>remember or care about who your predecessor was. (This is true even of Sidereals, aside from the &quot;no iconic banners at all&quot; thing.)<br /> <br /> The extent to which the character's past matters to his present has always been entirely a matter of what story the player wants to tell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure there were some 1st Age Swan-totem Lunar ambassadors - who after the Usurpation and bloodshed and suffering - would ditch the Swan and return as a glorious Lion (still a symbol of society and politics and governance - but now the mark of a King, not a Courtier). </div> </div> </div>For such a character, I would make his spirit shape wholly a Lion... but a lion which is the pure white color of the noble swan, with a mane and tail-tuft of downy feathers. (Wings optional and unnecessary.)<br /> <br /> The function of his new form clearly announces his new ferocity and warlike methods, but it still harkens back to his previous bearing. It shows that he hasn't completely forgotten the manners and ideals that used to be the cornerstone of his identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, I'm sure there has to be some 1st Age Tiger-totem Lunar barbarian - who spent centuries shedding blood, acting rashly, eventually forming relationships and watching them die - who in the 2nd Age resurfaces with a patient, peaceful, thoughtful Turtle-totem with a new life started in the far West. </div> </div> </div>Then his spirit shape is a turtle, but with the stripped patterns that helped the tiger blend in with his surroundings so well, and the sharp claws that wait patiently for the right time to be used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish I had cool inspirations for Chimera. </div> </div> </div>I didn't think I had any either, but it seems the ideas keep coming. Especially when answering prompts like yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-10-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:49:05-08:00","id":400916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably, the Tell will go back to its First Edition variability, where it didn't have to be a bestial feature. Like Beast Boy's green coloration. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I remember one of the developers or writers complaining about how the 2E version of the tell made it so that they had to make Raksi's hands a mutation instead of her tell if they wanted her to remain evocative of the thing she was inspired by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:23:20-08:00","id":400973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400907#post400907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, the Tell will go back to its First Edition variability, where it didn't have to be a bestial feature. Like Beast Boy's green coloration.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let crippling deformities be Tells, though, unless such a thing specifically prevented the Lunar from ever recovering from that deformity. The devs have said they've found a way to introduce Flaws into the game in a way they like, and I could see a Lunar take a Flaw as a Tell as easily as a physical &quot;mutation&quot; Merit.<br /> <br /> On which note, I want to be able to make a &quot;mutation&quot; into my Tell. I want to be able to choose a bull's horns, and always have the bull's horns in all of my forms (assuming that's what Tells still do), but almost no one can actually notice my horns without a really good Awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: And by &quot;mutation/Merit&quot;, I mean I want my Tell to be functionally weaponized horns that I can use to gore someone, even if they couldn't see my horns until their blood is coating them.<br /> <br /> So damn sick of animal feature Tells that were purely cosmetic. If someone can see wolf ears on my head, then those ears had better damn well give me keen hearing!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400916#post400916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure I remember one of the developers or writers complaining about how the 2E version of the tell made it so that they had to make Raksi's hands a mutation instead of her tell if they wanted her to remain evocative of the thing she was inspired by.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care at all about that specific example, because backward-bending fingers sounds stupid as hell. How awkward does that have to be?<br /> <br /> And what the hell does it have to do with her Spirit Shape? At least Red Jaw's scarred eye was a feature of his original human self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-10-2015, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:51:12-08:00","id":400999,"title":"","content":"Have we brought up Moonsilver Doomtrain yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:29:05-08:00","id":401599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400999#post400999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we brought up Moonsilver Doomtrain yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The real question is, can a Full Moon martial artist successfully suplex it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T06:23:27-08:00","id":401800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=400973#post400973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care at all about that specific example, because backward-bending fingers sounds stupid as hell. How awkward does that have to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC When Raksi was written, the tell wasn't forcibly a feature of your totem animal. It was a tell, like in poker (turned up to 11 because Lunar Exalted), where when she's not careful her tell is that her fingers bend backwards.<br /> It's not that her fingers <i>always</i> bend backwards, it's just that she's <i>so</i> double-jointed that it's a thing that happens. Some people bite their nails when stressed, some rub their necks when uncomfortable, some crack their knuckles out of akwardness, she bends her fingers backwards. It ain't no thang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-11-2015, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T06:52:42-08:00","id":401813,"title":"","content":"Raksi's Tell (backwards bending fingers) was a nod over to the Raksha of D&amp;D - horrible, beastlike man eating monsters whom (unlike their real versions in Hindu mythology) all possess backwards bending fingers while her totem form was a nod to the Jungle Book (monkey who lives in an ancient ruined city and kidnaps children).<br /> <br /> Eh, at the time, some people thought it was kind of clever (I did), but that was over a decade ago.<br /> <br /> And yeah, in 1st edition sometimes your Tell was just a weird feature, and while it could be a bestial trait related to your Spirit Shape, it could also be something more mundane, such as an unusual streak of hair or a weird colored eye, or it could be something downright inhuman like Raksi's hands, which would tend to bend backwards when she wasn't paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-11-2015, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:30:56-08:00","id":401832,"title":"","content":"Ma-Ha-Suchi's Tell was his voice like silver bells initially, up until 2e said your tell had to be a feature of your totem animal or somesuch, causing them to have to write a mutation for his weird voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:31:13-08:00","id":401837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=401800#post401800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC When Raksi was written, the tell wasn't forcibly a feature of your totem animal. It was a tell, like in poker (turned up to 11 because Lunar Exalted), where when she's not careful her tell is that her fingers bend backwards.<br /> It's not that her fingers <i>always</i> bend backwards, it's just that she's <i>so</i> double-jointed that it's a thing that happens. Some people bite their nails when stressed, some rub their necks when uncomfortable, some crack their knuckles out of akwardness, she bends her fingers backwards. It ain't no thang.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite explanation thus far about the Tell.<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;master shapeshifter has a flaw for some reason&quot; it becomes &quot;master shapeshifter has this one tick, this one habit, they never quite hide well&quot;. Instead of &quot;I shapeshifted but my disguise is fucked up&quot; it's more like &quot;my body can become anything, so yeah, sometimes I forget to reign it in&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like a dude in drag - and he's damn convincing - if not for a single flaw. Maybe he forgets to regulate the pitch in his voice at times. Or he walks funny. Or a tell-tale bulge. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:34:15-08:00","id":401862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=401813#post401813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi's Tell (backwards bending fingers) was a nod over to the Raksha of D&amp;D - horrible, beastlike man eating monsters whom (unlike their real versions in Hindu mythology) all possess backwards bending fingers while her totem form was a nod to the Jungle Book (monkey who lives in an ancient ruined city and kidnaps children).<br /> <br /> Eh, at the time, some people thought it was kind of clever (I did), but that was over a decade ago.<br /> <br /> And yeah, in 1st edition sometimes your Tell was just a weird feature, and while it could be a bestial trait related to your Spirit Shape, it could also be something more mundane, such as an unusual streak of hair or a weird colored eye, or it could be something downright inhuman like Raksi's hands, which would tend to bend backwards when she wasn't paying attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>The backward-bending hands were originally from Kolchak the Night Stalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:26:47-08:00","id":402017,"title":"","content":"Here's something that was brought up from the RPG.net discussion. Inspirations for Mental Attributes. We can imagine the visceral and primal feelings of both Physical and Social Attributes, but i'm hard pressed to find inspiration for Mental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:42:06-08:00","id":402061,"title":"","content":"Wits so sharp they make you bleed.<br /> Crazy like a FOX!<br /> An elephant never forgets... TO KILL!<br /> <br /> Senses... well those are pretty much covered already.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, John/Holden* had mentioned &quot;being smart <i>as</i> an elephant instead of smart <i>like</i> an elephant&quot;. Yet also that charms will be separate from animal-themed shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> For mental charms, I'd like to see some actual Moon themes (madness, lunacy, dreams, subconscious, inspiration, intuition)<br /> i.e. figuring things out while you sleep or are in altered states of consciousness, maybe even charms for getting bonuses from psychotropics. Delegating rolls into the subconscious (imagine Tony Stark going out to party only to be struck by THE ONE SOLUTION in the middle of drunken flirting.)<br /> <br /> And whatnot. Idunno.<br /> <br /> *(I already don't remember. Clearly, I am not an elephant)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:52:55-08:00","id":402085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=402061#post402061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wits so sharp they make you bleed.<br /> Crazy like a FOX!<br /> An elephant never forgets... TO KILL!</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely be happy to see more metaphorical or allegorical animal themes find their ways into the Lunar set, should that be in the cards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *(I already don't remember. Clearly, I am not an elephant) </div> </div> </div>I do! It was John. Thus, clearly I... Hunh. Well, my day just got a lot more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:37:45-08:00","id":402490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=402061#post402061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wits so sharp they make you bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sharper than that.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-code=\"TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TtE76BEvZ7o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:00:18-08:00","id":402523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=402490#post402490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sharper than that.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-code=\"TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TtE76BEvZ7o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>xD<br /> <br /> I got home after a grueling 12 hours of work. Exhausted, hungry, grumpy and dehydrated. This made the entirety of my day. All of it. And then some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:03:51-08:00","id":402525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=402490#post402490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sharper than that.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-code=\"TtE76BEvZ7o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TtE76BEvZ7o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It is amazing how terrible she is at talking with someone like an equal whose face she can't just burn off if things don't go her way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:18:52-08:00","id":402535,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, on the recurring topic of Alex Mercer the Lunar, reading back on Lunars 1e because i'm a masochist many charms straight up allow you to do Mercer things. Wicked claws, whipping limb, bladed arm (provided you have a blade) exoskeletal armor and even a bone shield.<br /> <br /> Same with stretchy arm guys allowing the twisting and elongation of body and limbs to dodge and extend reach.<br /> <br /> It's been so long, and many make so many claims that this dissonance comes from 2e, that I found it interesting when it's there clear as day in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:24:20-08:00","id":402542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=402535#post402535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, on the recurring topic of Alex Mercer the Lunar, reading back on Lunars 1e because i'm a masochist many charms straight up allow you to do Mercer things. Wicked claws, whipping limb, bladed arm (provided you have a blade) exoskeletal armor and even a bone shield.<br /> <br /> Same with stretchy arm guys allowing the twisting and elongation of body and limbs to dodge and extend reach.<br /> <br /> It's been so long, and many make so many claims that this dissonance comes from 2e, that I found it interesting when it's there clear as day in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is interesting, especially with the statements about how 1e Lunars had a very clearly-defined shapeshifting niche in the outline (compared to 2e). Maybe 1e Lunars were encouraged to be Mercer-Lunars in that way; 2e just allowed it by not narrowing down a thematic zone for them to sit in. I imagine 3e will have a very specific place for them but that place will not include Mercer effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-11-2015, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:41:34-08:00","id":402565,"title":"","content":"Claws, spines and whips do not Alex Mercer make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T03:40:41-08:00","id":403170,"title":"","content":"Mercer is probably closer to a Liminal in many ways, especially the fact that <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">he isn't actually Alex Mercer, but a composite being of which Mercer is the biggest part. The identity crisis, the <i>obligatory</i> inhumanity, and the monster-that-hunts-monsters part all feel very Liminal. Some of his abilities are Lunar, like the way he devours people to disguise as them, but his plot arc and overarching thematics feel more Liminal to me.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (Liminal murders the spotlight and takes its pieces to replace his eyes, activated!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T04:56:50-08:00","id":403187,"title":"","content":"I also think there's a whole load of potential from drawing on certain invertebrates. I myself would very much like a Lunar who is able to shoot their stomach from their mouth in the form of multiple filaments, ala the coral polyp, for the sake of eating people alive.<br /> <br /> As the other thread ultimately had to keep repeating, one can probably manage a lot of the things Prototype was doing without needing to get off message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T07:42:21-08:00","id":403311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403170#post403170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the way he devours people to disguise as them</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure Flesh Charms (and Mercer is obviously the vengeance/violence-oriented Flesh Aspect) will allow Liminals to streamline their chop-shopping to the point where they do what Mercer does, and just straight up absorb people into themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:19:06-08:00","id":403373,"title":"","content":"I kind of have a question to the forum.<br /> <br /> Recently, I watched The Little Mermaid for the first time in half a decade, so my question is...<br /> <br /> Is Ursula a good inspiration for a Lunar?<br /> <br /> Outside of having a rather obvious animal theme, she barters with someone for a part of their appearance and I like the idea of a Lunar bartering with someone for their voice, or their eyes or their face, it fits the Trickster part of the Lunars. She even has shapeshifting abilities. Theo nly thing that's really missing is that she's a barbarian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:46:03-08:00","id":403408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403373#post403373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Ursula a good inspiration for a Lunar?<br /> <br /> Outside of having a rather obvious animal theme, she barters with someone for a part of their appearance and I like the idea of a Lunar bartering with someone for their voice, or their eyes or their face, it fits the Trickster part of the Lunars. She even has shapeshifting abilities. Theo nly thing that's really missing is that she's a barbarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she'd make a fantastic No-Moon with Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique / Wondrous Lunar Transformation and some sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:47:07-08:00","id":403409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403373#post403373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of have a question to the forum.<br /> <br /> Recently, I watched The Little Mermaid for the first time in half a decade, so my question is...<br /> <br /> Is Ursula a good inspiration for a Lunar?<br /> <br /> Outside of having a rather obvious animal theme, she barters with someone for a part of their appearance and I like the idea of a Lunar bartering with someone for their voice, or their eyes or their face, it fits the Trickster part of the Lunars. She even has shapeshifting abilities. Theo nly thing that's really missing is that she's a barbarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's usually taken as a dynamite representation of Cecelyne and Kimbery Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:35:46-08:00","id":403435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403409#post403409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's usually taken as a dynamite representation of Cecelyne and Kimbery Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, you can use Lunar charms to give others mutations - and not strictly animal ones either (unless your ST is house-ruling to impose their fur-society tastes). This means a No Moon could use controlled wyld exposure (via the charm) to make you Mute or grant you extra limbs (coincidentally, the +2 legs are Ariel's first two).<br /> <br /> So yes, you can do it as an Infernal - but don't rule Lunars out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T14:01:47-08:00","id":403675,"title":"","content":"Again from RPG.net<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;A fox's teeth are very sharp. And with a flick of her tail, she was gone.&quot;</i> -Neil Gaiman, <i>Sandman: The Dream Hunters</i><br /> <br /> (Incidentally, as much as it looks like I'm supporting the no-cannibalism-necessary position here, I'm really just being a contratrian smartass; in reality I am the most hardline proponent of cannibalism-only skin-thieving for Lunars. The point is, you don't need to be rampaging and blood-soaked to be a cannibal skin-thief.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hooray! I am not alone!<br /> I know I know, I should make an account and post over there. Contrary to here though, I won't have such a <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">prestigious</span> post count.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(blue is sarcasm, right?)</span><br /> <br /> Edit: I do think that &quot;Eating&quot; is central to Lunars; and by association, Eating People.<br /> <br /> I see them as the glowing eyes in the darkness, the slavering maw that devours those who venture into the forest at night. And with nothing but a whisper, they disappear - into the forest, into the crowd, into the flock of birds. They are the monsters parents tell cautionary tales about. The stalkers in the night. And a big part of that is the fear of Getting Eaten.<br /> <br /> That they steal your shape is to add to the horror of being consumed. Their theme, to me, isn't &quot;Generic Shapeshifting&quot; so much as &quot;Eating and replacing you&quot;. And that monster is within them all. The unstoppable berserker that cleaves through your caravan-mates, the sly drug-dealer that introduces cheap drugs into your city and keeps a strangle-hold on poor, the silky-smooth high-society diplomat that's relentless-as-a-crocodile-mid-death-roll in his/her pursuit of policy. He might be proud and loyal, she might be lithe and inoffensive, but they <i>all</i> can and will <i>fucking eat you</i> the moment you rub them the wrong way. (individually they might not, they, specifically, might frown on cannibalism, but <i>you</i> don't know that. what you know is that <i>Lunars eat people</i>. And you just blew one's cover.)<br /> <br /> This is what attracts me to Lunars and why I play them. Not &quot;let's play cards for your face&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-12-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T17:55:33-08:00","id":403934,"title":"","content":"A thought on the possibilities for Intelligence Charms: while reading about the king cobra, there was a note on how they use their intelligence in the course of hunting prey. It got me wondering &quot;what is the intelligent behaviour of a cobra&quot;, which led to the supposition &quot;probably being able to form predictions of the movement patterns of prey, especially distant prey which their keen eyesight can percieve and which could move quite a distance during the approach, as well as approach patterns to catch prey off-guard&quot;. From there, I also considered observations in the behaviour of octipuses, such as escaping through tanks by slipping through tiny gaps, and apparent communication through changing colour patterns, even in multiple directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T20:43:46-08:00","id":404069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403170#post403170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Liminal murders the spotlight and takes its pieces to replace his eyes, activated!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope when 3E comes out, this can be a thing. Lunars need competition in the &quot;all threads are lunar threads&quot; arena, and Liminals sound awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T01:47:34-08:00","id":404281,"title":"","content":"Silly mortal; all threads are lunar threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T04:22:09-08:00","id":404373,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm torn about something:<br /> <br /> I've got more ideas for Intelligence Charms, even one that postulate mechanics, but I'm put off by the whole thing where the writers are unwilling or not permitted to use ideas that they see publically displayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T05:50:55-08:00","id":404407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=403170#post403170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Liminal murders the spotlight and takes its pieces to replace his eyes, activated!)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404281#post404281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly mortal; all threads are lunar threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Threads are just Lunar Threads stealing the shapes of Liminals.<br /> <br /> ... huh, I wonder if that's gonna be a thing. Does a Liminal who's an amalgam of parts count as a single shape? Can they be Sacred Hunted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404373#post404373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm torn about something:<br /> <br /> I've got more ideas for Intelligence Charms, even one that postulate mechanics, but I'm put off by the whole thing where the writers are unwilling or not permitted to use ideas that they see publically displayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you... post under the GPL license? Though I'm not sure that would do it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-13-2015, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T06:40:03-08:00","id":404433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404407#post404407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Liminal who's an amalgam of parts count as a single shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaphysically, probably yes. It would be a little goofy otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404407#post404407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they be Sacred Hunted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends if they have blood, maybe. I dunno. Was Frankenstein's monster truly alive, or just a horrific simulacrum of what it means to be alive?<br /> <br /> Best case, you're still just going to get their physical shape. But that's all you're going to get if you eat a DB, and then you need to rely on your Charms to provide any weird effects to be convincing (though not many people are going to question an obviously-Aspect-marked DB).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T07:56:37-08:00","id":404469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404433#post404433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaphysically, probably yes. It would be a little goofy otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well of course they're one entity, I mean specifically for being able to shapeshift into them. One of the possible answers is &quot;You can't Sacred Hunt a pile of corpse parts, no matter how magically animated it is&quot;<br /> or &quot;You get the shape of the person who contributed the heart&quot; .. but that'd be weird and is imo unlikely.<br /> Chances are that the official answer will be &quot;You ge the Liminal's shape&quot;. I just think it'd be funny/neat if you couldn't because they're too strange, to a point that even Lunar Shapeshifting Magic goes &quot;dude, what the fuck?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-13-2015, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T10:19:31-08:00","id":404661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404373#post404373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm torn about something:<br /> <br /> I've got more ideas for Intelligence Charms, even one that postulate mechanics, but I'm put off by the whole thing where the writers are unwilling or not permitted to use ideas that they see publically displayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry about this. You can pretty much trust the devs not to read things that will impede their ability to write the game, or at least not to tell anyone if they do. (If you <i>want</i> them to read it you can get a release form from OPP and send it as a writing submission once the game is out, but then you probably can't post it here.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T11:00:01-08:00","id":404708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404373#post404373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm torn about something:<br /> <br /> I've got more ideas for Intelligence Charms, even one that postulate mechanics, but I'm put off by the whole thing where the writers are unwilling or not permitted to use ideas that they see publically displayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't checked the terms of use for this forum, but I recall on the old forum, there was some legal boilerplate that stated that WW (or their parent company, whose name I can't recall at the moment) owned all the content posted on the forums. If this forum has an equivalent to that boilerplate, it should be fine to post ideas, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T11:22:51-08:00","id":404762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404708#post404708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div