path.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T11:26:28-08:00","id":404774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can pretty much trust the devs not to read things that will impede their ability to write the game, or at least not to tell anyone if they do. (If you want them to read it you can get a release form from OPP and send it as a writing submission once the game is out, but then you probably can't post it here.)</div> </div> </div> </div> You are tearing me apart, forum!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T17:41:29-08:00","id":405345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=404708#post404708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't checked the terms of use for this forum, but I recall on the old forum, there was some legal boilerplate that stated that WW (or their parent company, whose name I can't recall at the moment) owned all the content posted on the forums. If this forum has an equivalent to that boilerplate, it should be fine to post ideas, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming Q4 2016, the Scroll of Jen Header Art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T17:51:35-08:00","id":405351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=405345#post405345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming Q4 2016, the Scroll of Jen Header Art.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Jen got paid for the contributions, I'd buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T20:16:01-08:00","id":405425,"title":"","content":"I want to be able to be this as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/-vyA1tO8bX8?t=1m7s\" data-code=\"-vyA1tO8bX8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-vyA1tO8bX8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T21:13:38-08:00","id":405446,"title":"","content":"Even though it's about dying bravely, this song contains very Lunar imagery, at least in my opinion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uZk1CvsDSZc\" data-code=\"uZk1CvsDSZc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uZk1CvsDSZc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T13:42:17-08:00","id":408168,"title":"","content":"Moving a discussion over from another thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407785-if-you-can-ask-the-dev-s-one-question?p=408107#post408107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm as confused by this statement as much as I was by your original question. The Devs have said that you can play a Lunar with very little shapeshifting at all if that's what you choose. He'll just focus on other things like Evocations, Sorcery, Martial Arts (and these are just the combat principles). They've also said they're going to have a unique ability to claim a &quot;dominion&quot; and have some power over the area they've claimed. Plenty of ways to play a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though for the life of me, I don't know why anyone would want to play a Lunar that didn't shapeshift. Seems your ignore something cool and unique to your class of exalts just because &quot;I don't wanna&quot;! Why not play a different exalt altogether then? </div> </div> </div>We have different notions of what is cool and unique. The only kind of shapeshifter I really want to play is the Alex Mercer type, and Morke has shown himself to be pretty hostile to that concept for this edition. Lunars appear to be stuck using their shapeshifting only to turn into animals now, with the tradeoff being that animals are more powerful and have unique abilities now. That's great, but I'm still not interested in playing Beastboy.<br /> <br /> Now, what I think is <i>really</i> cool about Lunars are their attribute charms. I love the idea of being able to apply Dexterity charms to every weapon I lay hands on and being the omni-tactical battle hydra to match the Solar who specialized in swordplay or archery. I want those charms, and right now Lunars are the only way to get them without being a cyborg in another dimension (or an Exigent, whose splat probably won't be out until after several months after the Lunar splatbook drops).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T13:57:16-08:00","id":408177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408168#post408168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only kind of shapeshifter I really want to play is the Alex Mercer type, and Morke has shown himself to be pretty hostile to that concept for this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely accurate.<br /> <br /> More that that type of shapeshifter is not inherently Lunar in theme. It's more Liminal, or a particular kind of Exigent.<br /> <br /> So you could play a Mercer shapeshifter, but the Lunar chassis is not the chassis you want to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T14:21:38-08:00","id":408188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408168#post408168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(or an Exigent, whose splat probably won't be out until after several months after the Lunar splatbook drops).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, you've got nothing to worry about on that front. The splat release order is mostly a mystery, but they've definitely confirmed how it starts off:<br /> Solars -&gt; Dragonblooded -&gt; Exigents -&gt; ????","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:08:36-08:00","id":408336,"title":"","content":"I do belive I did an entrie thread on the &quot;Prototype as Luars&quot; topic, in which I explained how that kind of shifting is in theme for Lunars, as long as wyou're willing to do some refluffing.<br /> <br /> James more so than Mercer, but I did make reasonable fakes for Alex's weapon powers-which are pretty Viable if that &quot;Augment natural weapons with Moonsilver Claws&quot; strenth charm sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:21:55-08:00","id":408345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408336#post408336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do belive I did an entrie thread on the &quot;Prototype as Luars&quot; topic, in which I explained how that kind of shifting is in theme for Lunars, as long as wyou're willing to do some refluffing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to beat a dead horse, but: maybe so in 2e, but not in 3e.<br /> <br /> Myself, I am <i>quite </i>excited to see how closely I can evoke that stuff with Liminals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:54:07-08:00","id":408369,"title":"","content":"I still don't see any meaningful difference between the two beyond minor details that would necessarily be changed when making a character inspired by another character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:57:51-08:00","id":408388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408369#post408369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see any meaningful difference between the two beyond minor details that would necessarily be changed when making a character inspired by another character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of it will be clarified when we see some example Charms for each splat. <br /> <br /> Because yeah at this point we are talking blind about the super-abstract, having no solid mechanical frames of reference relevant to the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:43:52-08:00","id":408443,"title":"","content":"Well chimerism was said to be more of a choice (a Lunar that uses portions of multiple animal transformations). That could be kind of like Mercer. Also, while this shouldn't need to be said, it's your game. Run it however you want to get the most enjoyment out of it. The Exigent book is suppose to outline charm creation. Should be easy to mod some Lunar charms to be more &quot;Mercer-like&quot; in usage.<br /> <br /> On a side note, Lunars now have little to no Wyld taint in 3E. Perhaps your particular Lunar was Wyld tainted, and it made your transformations a bit more like Prototype. John's comments about not liking Prototype for Lunars was more for the general theme of all Lunars. PCs can and should be unique, so make up a fun back story (ie Wyld tainted, ate a weird creature, got sapped by some 1st Age magic talisman, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 02-16-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:36:03-08:00","id":408513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408443#post408443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well chimerism was said to be more of a choice (a Lunar that uses portions of multiple animal transformations). That could be kind of like Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, chimerism sounds like it's heading toward being like in 1e, only without the horrible punishment mechanics and more control over what the result looks like. So, kind of like Perfected Hybrid Interaction, only it gives you more choices instead of blowing the door open and letting you go absolutely crazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, while this shouldn't need to be said, it's your game. Run it however you want to get the most enjoyment out of it. The Exigent book is suppose to outline charm creation. Should be easy to mod some Lunar charms to be more &quot;Mercer-like&quot; in usage. </div> </div> </div>I hope that we get the names and themes of those other two Lunar-related Exaltations soon. Pressure on the Lunars still mounts yet, it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a side note, Lunars now have little to no Wyld taint in 3E. Perhaps your particular Lunar was Wyld tainted, and it made your transformations a bit more like Prototype. John's comments about not liking Prototype for Lunars was more for the general theme of all Lunars. PCs can and should be unique, so make up a fun back story (ie Wyld tainted, ate a weird creature, got sapped by some 1st Age magic talisman, etc). </div> </div> </div>Probably no Wyld taint at all. We've been told that the caste shifting has to do with internal changes, rather than the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T06:49:25-08:00","id":410046,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I didn't make a thread for this so I'll just repost the whole thing. Surely when you all witness my genius, all the problems with Lunars will be fixed <i>forever</i>. It's a good thing this forum doesn't have spoilers anymore or I might actually have to hide this and then you all wouldn't be forces to look at this. Haha, good thing.<br /> <br /> Here goes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Caste Terminology<br /> <br /> It is important to note that the Lunar Exalted are not the Solar Exalted. The Sidereal and their Auspices are not the Solar Exalted and the Terrestrial and their Aspects are not the Solar Exalted. The Infernal and the Abyssal Exalted and their Castes, in fact, ARE the Solar Exalted, in strange twisted ways and share their terminology for delineating loose roles of one another. The Lunar Exalted are not the Solar Exalted and nor should they have their words.<br /> <br /> (One could justify that the Alchemicals, prototype of all the Exalted, do not so much as borrow the Solar terminology as the Solar borrow from them. If not, one might consider also changing the name used by the Champions from Caste to Class, ie Excessively Righteous Blossom, Moonsilver Class.)<br /> <br /> What the Lunar follow then are the Phases of the Moon. Luna Ambiguus Aeternum, the Forever Changing Moon, flows through each of these Phases to there and gone again and the halfway points between and her Chosen may take up one of these aspects. The same with Sol and his Chosen, even the Night being the aspect when the Unconquered crawls under Creation and dodges, sneak and runs through things he'd rather not. Only the Chosen of the Maidens take up a whole goddess, such as the Five are almost One made more so ten eyes can feast upon Fate as needed.<br /> <br /> (The suggestions of this Paradigm refer to one another as if they were one block suggestion. While true, in the technical sense, choice bits may be pulled out from them and easily applied without everything else. Below are suggestions for expanding the number of 'Phases' and changing the Phase Marks. This can just as easily be used if they're still called 'Castes' and 'Phase' can be used without any of the below.)<br /> <br /> Extra Castes<br /> <br /> The Moon shifts through a number of Phases. There is the Full Moon, when Luna shines in her full and violent glory. There is the Half Moon, when coyly does Luna veil herself as if a courtesan ready to entreat with words. There is the New Moon, when Luna turns her face away completely to delve in forbidden thoughts and perspectives. In between, there are others, the Gibbous Moon when Luna's full terror is there but she holds back just a fraction, stay her hand for just long enough, to use her words before she uses her fists, or when she is suited for speech but ready for violence. The Crescent Moon, when Luna has nearly gone to her private darkness but shows her face upon the world still or when she is still a socialite but of a mind wandering into black thoughts. The Hidden Moon, when Luna is not just shrouded in shadows but completely gone, not speaking or showing herself to the world at all but stewing in her private thoughts, ready to explode forward in her terrible might.<br /> <br /> (As this paragraph may demonstrate, using 'Moon' rather then 'Phase' or 'Caste' may be as valid an option. It would certainly be strange but rhythmically fitting.)<br /> <br /> These inbetween Phases come when the Chosen chooses all their Attributes as if they were Favored but treats them afterwards as his Phase attributes. With five choices and nine possibilities, the Lunar's Phase is decided by which of three categories, Mind, Body and Face, he favors the most. When a tie is had, one of the 'Middle Moons' is taken up. But the nature of one of the Middle Moons, less absolute then the Prime Moons, transient that they are, is harder to pin. What does Luna give up first when she goes from the Full Moon to the Half Moon, taking up the Gibbous Moon, Violent Strength or Cheating Dexterity? What does she take last, Heartfelt Charisma or Unseen Appearance? And what one thing of Mind does she take, Changing Intelligence or Ant Toppling Wits? That's just a metaphor, of course, Luna has all of them and more, but it represents the problem of trying to personify the Middle Moons handedly.<br /> <br /> (For the Prime Moons, there are 15 different combinations for each Phase. For the Middle Moons, there are 27 possible combinations each.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Strength Charisma Intelligence<br /> Dexterity Manipulation Wits<br /> Stamina Appearance Perception <br /> <br /> <br /> The sobriquet of the Lunar Phases are as follow, in order from Full Moon to Hidden: Moon Warrior, Dark Paladin, Silver Bard, Witch Priest, Argent Sorcerer and Night Fighter.<br /> <br /> (In a Creation without the Middle Moons, they may be, from Full to No, Moon Warrior, Silver Priest and Dark Sorcerer. In such a Creation, the Half Moon would be the Changing Moon.)<br /> <br /> Caste Marks<br /> <br /> The Lunars are not the Solars, that much cannot be stressed enough. As all the Celestial do though, they bear the mark of their patron, shaped by their Phase, as a tiara crown on their brow. The Lunar Phase Marks are not just shining beacons of silvery white light but of light devouring darkness, glowing with shadows.<br /> <br /> ( <a href=\"http://imgur.com/M86RovE\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/M86RovE</a> )<br /> <br /> Each Phase Mark is dropped upon a spot of darkness just as the Silver Chair is oft backdropped against the black night. The Full Moon differs from the Zenith by a triplicate of light devouring dots that replicates the eternally surprised face inexplicably carved into the Silver Chair. The New Moon differs from the Night by being a broken ring of twin crescents. The rest are so different in their basic shape but further drive their shared uniqueness by the interplay of light and shadow. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:30:45-08:00","id":410645,"title":"","content":"&quot;Glowing with shadows&quot; sounds more like an Abyssal thing than a Lunar thing =/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:56:00-08:00","id":410662,"title":"","content":"I think Abyssals can share.<br /> <br /> Part-dark and part-light is so very Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:28:38-08:00","id":410695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=410645#post410645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Glowing with shadows&quot; sounds more like an Abyssal thing than a Lunar thing =/</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Luna wears a cloak of Night. Abyssals come from a lightless place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:20:33-08:00","id":410870,"title":"","content":"No Moons' anima literally surrounds them with shadows. They're the caste of the darkness when the moon is hidden. I think it's pretty fitting for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:42:23-08:00","id":417005,"title":"","content":"Back in First Edition, Lunars didn't just have Armor-Forming Technique and Claws of the Silver Moon, they also had things like Flying Squirrel Method for growing gliding skin flaps between your arms and legs, and Panther Stride Style, for making whatever form you were using slimmer and more aerodynamic for better running speed.<br /> <br /> But they also had Hide-Toughening Essence, and other glowy, non-physical, &quot;purely magical&quot; effects.<br /> <br /> During one out of my hundreds of attempts to fix the Lunar Charmset, I thought that it would be good to allow Lunars to buy two Charms for any effect that could be justified with physical shapeshifting; one for the physical transformation, and one for the &quot;purely magical&quot; effect, just like the pair of Armor-Forming Technique and Hide-Toughening Essence. The purely magical effect would be less obvious, but also less effective.<br /> <br /> But that was back in the days when animals weren't worth shit for turning into. You turned into a bird when you needed to fly or a fish to swim, but cheetahs and horses had poor traits for running, so why bother using them except for off-screen travel? If there was any on-screen action, you wanted Deadly Beastman Transformation.<br /> <br /> Well now animal shapeshifting is finally being made competitive with DBT by making animals awesome. Now Lunar players WILL want to turn into horses and cats for groundspeed.<br /> <br /> Which is why I hope that Panther Stride Stance and its kind will not return. Perhaps not even Armor-Forming Technique.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar wants living armor, should he be able to grow it on any form he pleases? Hybrid Body Rearrangement let you slap armor and wings and fire-breathing on anything you became, and it really stopped mattering what form you had.<br /> <br /> Hide-Toughening Essence, on the other hand, improves the soak that the Lunar already has without a physical transformation, and thus enhances rather than muddles any form the Lunar might wear. Yes, his octopus form becomes hardier, but it's still an octopus rather than an armor-plated cephalopod.<br /> <br /> Claws of the Silver Moon, as the last Edition, likewise merely improved the traits of the Lunar's existing natural weaponry rather than growing new bits. You don't grow horns or claws on the octopus, but its beak bites more sharply and its tentacles lash like razor whips. The form is very much still distinctly an octopus, but it is now an octopus of legend; a beast of mythical power.<br /> <br /> Let Heart's Blood shapeshifting handle Lunar shapeshifting. Let the legendary power come from the Charms. Say &quot;No&quot; to Hybrid Body Rearrangement, Armor-Forming Technique and Flying Squirrel Method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T21:19:06-08:00","id":421200,"title":"","content":"You know, if a lot of the illusion-y effects are being removed from the Lunar charmset, I think they would work <i>really</i> well as Evocations on a set of moonsilver armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:43:17-08:00","id":421528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=408388#post408388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because yeah at this point we are talking blind about the super-abstract, having no solid mechanical frames of reference relevant to the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that statement sum up this whole forum right now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T05:26:09-08:00","id":421624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421528#post421528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that statement sum up this whole forum right now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Not really. They've generally spoiled some mechanics, and we know that at least some other splats' themes aren't really veering away from what they've been in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:40:16-08:00","id":421744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421200#post421200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if a lot of the illusion-y effects are being removed from the Lunar charmset, I think they would work <i>really</i> well as Evocations on a set of moonsilver armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect some of the illusion-y stuff in Lunars may still stick around in their set in a different form, but this is an interesting thought. I'm definitely curious to hear more about moonsilver's associations and the sorts of Evocations one can pull out of artifacts made from it. With Lunars emphasizing the physicality, I had wondered if the MM's Evocations might focus more strictly on the physical side to reflect that. Which, as an idea, worried me a smidge; I was having some trouble coming up with interesting things to do with that. Making illusions one of the options for moonsilver Evocations makes sense to me; as a natural complement to native Lunar capabilities, it certainly feels like they'd get more out of it. As a side benefit, it could also satisfy those who are disappointed that illusions aren't really something that native Lunar magic will do in EX3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 02-27-2015, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:57:32-08:00","id":421755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421744#post421744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect some of the illusion-y stuff in Lunars may still stick around in their set in a different form, but this is an interesting thought. I'm definitely curious to hear more about moonsilver's associations and the sorts of Evocations one can pull out of artifacts made from it. With Lunars emphasizing the physicality, I had wondered if the MM's Evocations might focus more strictly on the physical side to reflect that. Which, as an idea, worried me a smidge; I was having some trouble coming up with interesting things to do with that. Making illusions one of the options for moonsilver Evocations makes sense to me; as a natural complement to native Lunar capabilities, it certainly feels like they'd get more out of it. As a side benefit, it could also satisfy those who are disappointed that illusions aren't really something that native Lunar magic will do in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of that stuff, and the discussion on how it would work, reminds me a bit of Devotions or Disciplines I saw <i>somewhere </i>in the Blood &amp; Smoke reboot for Vampire: the Requiem (specifically the &quot;look like the person your target most expects to see/most wants to see&quot; Lunar Charms). I'm poring over my books...ah, here we go.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 1 and 4 - Face in the Crowd and Familiar Stranger. Ah, it's not quite as extensive as the Lunars <i>Glories</i> Charms that do something similar, because it's more of great impersonation and observing social cues in response to it than it is reaching out to project an illusion onto the world that affects everyone who sees it differently, but it's a way to do it.<br /> <br /> Now the actual illusion stuff...I might just draft that up in a bit, in broad strokes, to see how it might look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:07:40-08:00","id":421762,"title":"","content":"If their charmset reintegrates shapeshifting, which I hope it does since it doesn't need to cater to Eclipses anymore (I'll never stop beating that horse), I'm hoping that their charms will work <i>through</i> shape-shifting (which basically means I want the exact opposite of what Sunder posted up-thread. Though honestly, I'd be happy with any engaging and thematically-consistent presentation of Lunars).<br /> <br /> I don't want shifting to be restricted to Heart's Blood. I <i>want</i> Tool-Hand Technique and Hybrid Body Rearrangement. <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:lunars-and-cannibalism\" target=\"_blank\">And cannibalism.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:36:30-08:00","id":421789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421762#post421762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll never stop beating that horse\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>What did the poor thing ever do to you?<br /> <br /> No, seriously, did you, <i>personally</i>, have a game ruined by Eclipse Charm-share? Even a session?<br /> <br /> I certainly didn't - in a game that spanned 2e, had no less than three Eclipse PCs, and tangled itself up in plots, metaplots, and bad mechanics, <i>not once</i> did the Eclipses present a problem by learning other people's Charms.<br /> <br /> In fact, their <i>other</i> anima power caused a lot more problems - the group's Zenith straight-up <i>murdered</i> the Eclipse who'd made an oath with a Fiend. I had a game session devolve into a <i>two-hour argument over Black Mirror Shintai</i>, but never so much as a misunderstanding came from Charmshare.<br /> <br /> So tell us how it ruined your game or <i>please</i> quit complaining; I've had a long night and I won't be getting any sleep before having to go work again, so my tolerance for echo-chamber bullshit is somewhat low today. If it <i>has</i> truly destroyed a game of yours, I apologize, but if not, drop the cudgel and let the corpse be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:52:48-08:00","id":421819,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\">I am hopeful that the disappearance of a thing that held them back in the past will help them be better in the future.</a><br /> And no. I won't. But I appreciate your politeness.<br /> <br /> Edit: TL;DR<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So he wrote the entire Lunar Charm set around the idea of &quot;Solar Eclipses should be able to learn these without breaking their own thematics&quot; and then shuffled <i>anything</i> that would be counter to Solar thematics into the Knacks system. But because he was focusing on the dichotomy of generic-stuff-in-the-Charms vs. specific-stuff-in-the-Knacks, and he had already established that Knacks were about shapeshifting, he was locked in a conceptual blind alley of &quot;The only specific stuff Lunars get is shapeshifting.&quot; The Lunar Charms came out very generic, and intentionally so.. </div> </div> </div>Their charms being generic was by design. So that Solars wouldn't break out of theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:53:06-08:00","id":421820,"title":"","content":"As a resident Lunar non-fan, who is going to delude himself into think that will somehow add a level of objectivity in evaluating what Lunars NEED vs what someone might WANT for or of Lunars. A fundamental issue has always, to me, lain at the heart of what will make or break Lunars the same way the base systems of the corebook will make or break everything that proceeds from it.<br /> <br /> Namely. If someone who has never heard of Exalted hung out with me and I started to talk about the game world to them. If asked what is the fundamental theme of Solars and Solar Charms by that person. I feel confident I could not only give them a short description but I could also give a range of mythic examples to illuminate that description. Lunars.......not even one iota in any meaningful way. I say meaningful because yes you can toss out sentences that involve stuff like &quot;mumblemumblemumbleSHAPESHIFTING!mumblemumbleLIKEA BEAR!.&quot; it's just highlighting the issue. Give me THAT before you start going into Mercers/#FuckEclipses2k15/HeartsBlood/etc and you've just saved Lunars finally after two editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:55:05-08:00","id":421822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421789#post421789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the poor thing ever do to you?<br /> <br /> No, seriously, did you, <i>personally</i>, have a game ruined by Eclipse Charm-share? Even a session?<br /> <br /> I certainly didn't - in a game that spanned 2e, had no less than three Eclipse PCs, and tangled itself up in plots, metaplots, and bad mechanics, <i>not once</i> did the Eclipses present a problem by learning other people's Charms.<br /> <br /> In fact, their <i>other</i> anima power caused a lot more problems - the group's Zenith straight-up <i>murdered</i> the Eclipse who'd made an oath with a Fiend. I had a game session devolve into a <i>two-hour argument over Black Mirror Shintai</i>, but never so much as a misunderstanding came from Charmshare.<br /> <br /> So tell us how it ruined your game or <i>please</i> quit complaining; I've had a long night and I won't be getting any sleep before having to go work again, so my tolerance for echo-chamber bullshit is somewhat low today. If it <i>has</i> truly destroyed a game of yours, I apologize, but if not, drop the cudgel and let the corpse be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, chill. If anything, the dead horse is being beaten because of <i>overreactions</i> to the Eclipse Charmshare. As I recall the situation, the writer/developer at the time explicitly wanted to keep Lunar shapeshifting out of Eclipse hands, and the way he decided to do it was to move it out of their Charmset and into Knacks. This was a contributing factor in the blandness of the 2e Lunar Charmset. <i>That</i> was the reason for Fata-Ku's remark.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or see the link in Fata-Ku's response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Sidereal'd. 02-27-2015, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:02:04-08:00","id":421834,"title":"","content":"Bland Charms (and not just Lunar ones!) can be laid at the feet of Charm-share, yes, but they never killed someone's game, as far as I can tell. There are far worse things to latch onto and ride into the ground. Bland Charms isn't even fifth on my list of &quot;What was wrong with Lunars 2e,&quot; mind.<br /> <br /> And an overreaction to something perceived as a problem doesn't mean the base thing was necessarily a problem - if a person physically assaults me over my choice of candy bar, is it my fault for having bought the candy bar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:10:48-08:00","id":421853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421834#post421834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And an overreaction to something perceived as a problem doesn't mean the base thing was necessarily a problem - if a person physically assaults me over my choice of candy bar, is it my fault for having bought the candy bar?</div> </div> </div> </div>... I've mentioned Charm-share 3 times in the last month. Has any of those times caused you grievous injury or harm?<br /> Hell I'm not even going on about it, It's a passing remark in a sentence that's wholly <i>not about it</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bland Charms (and not just Lunar ones!) can be laid at the feet of Charm-share, yes, but they never killed someone's game, as far as I can tell. There are far worse things to latch onto and ride into the ground. </div> </div> </div>So? Sexism hasn't ruined my life (or any of my games) in any way, that doesn't prevent me from personally wanting it to go.<br /> The &quot;it doesn't affect you&quot; argument isn't a valid one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:11:23-08:00","id":421854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421834#post421834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bland Charms (and not just Lunar ones!) can be laid at the feet of Charm-share, yes, but they never killed someone's game, as far as I can tell. There are far worse things to latch onto and ride into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't the bedrock of why Lunars have been a jumble of patchwork ideas for so long but I have to agree with Gaius. So much of Lunars has been bland because there's never been a coherency on what they ARE really save in the most vague of expressions. In and of itself it might not kill a game per say. But pile it onto stuff like &quot;I don't always make sly references to the CWoD but when I do so badly, I do it with Lunars.&quot;, What is best in life Lunar-Conan? &quot;Rape and hating civilization!&quot;(this is a reference to the first edition Lunars book and I mean it as a fairly angry and more than fairly serious indictment of the book), and 2nd editions Society Built Painfully Obviously on Not Altering the Setting but Throwing the Lunar Dog Spirit Shape a Bone. It certainly helps kill Lunar fan enthusiasm, or in my case, ever getting interested in the splat in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:21:27-08:00","id":421867,"title":"","content":"Fuck it, I mistook your post for that of someone who's been particularly more anti-Eclipse in general, and when you said you weren't gonna stop beating that horse, I took it to mean you were gonna keep bitching about Eclipses at every opportunity in a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> This is why you shouldn't forum when you're tired, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:24:36-08:00","id":421874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421867#post421867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck it, I mistook your post for that of someone who's been particularly more anti-Eclipse in general, and when you said you weren't gonna stop beating that horse, I took it to mean you were gonna keep bitching about Eclipses at every opportunity in a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> This is why you shouldn't forum when you're tired, folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Nah. Eclipses are pretty much my favorite Solars to begin with :P<br /> (the wont-stop-beating-the-horse thing was as a joke, because it's been brought up a couple times lately)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:35:49-08:00","id":421884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421762#post421762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If their charmset reintegrates shapeshifting, which I hope it does since it doesn't need to cater to Eclipses anymore (I'll never stop beating that horse), I'm hoping that their charms will work <i>through</i> shape-shifting (which basically means I want the exact opposite of what Sunder posted up-thread. Though honestly, I'd be happy with any engaging and thematically-consistent presentation of Lunars).<br /> <br /> I don't want shifting to be restricted to Heart's Blood. I <i>want</i> Tool-Hand Technique and Hybrid Body Rearrangement. <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:lunars-and-cannibalism\" target=\"_blank\">And cannibalism.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>While I really don't want either of those Charms to return, I'm definitely okay with Humble Mouse Shape and Wondrous Lunar Transformation becoming Charms again, rather than staying Knacks.<br /> <br /> So long as the &quot;quick-transformation&quot; Charms are a tree-branch by themselves that any Lunar can snatch up without having to buy some entangled general-speed enhancing Dexterity Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:15:13-08:00","id":421971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421884#post421884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as the &quot;quick-transformation&quot; Charms are a tree-branch by themselves that any Lunar can snatch up without having to buy some entangled general-speed enhancing Dexterity Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, for the record, I'm not <i>against</i> charms like Hide-Toughening Essence, it should definitely be an option, because sometimes you're a cat that's getting stomped and need to survive <i>without</i> drawing attention to the fact that you're a body-snatching abomination, or whatnot.<br /> <br /> But I'm in it for the cannibalistic shape-stealing horrors that stalk the outskirts of the town at night, so while I wouldn't describe it as &quot;body horror&quot; (I'm <u>not</u> advocating for The Thing), some levels of &quot;what the fuck&quot; would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like to be able to make an Angler-Fish trapper that, while in DBT, can shoot octopus tentacles out of his stomach-mounted Hideous Maw to grapple and reel in his opponents, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:34:42-08:00","id":421986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421971#post421971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, for the record, I'm not <i>against</i> charms like Hide-Toughening Essence, it should definitely be an option, because sometimes you're a cat that's getting stomped and need to survive <i>without</i> drawing attention to the fact that you're a body-snatching abomination, or whatnot.<br /> <br /> But I'm in it for the cannibalistic shape-stealing horrors that stalk the outskirts of the town at night, so while I wouldn't describe it as &quot;body horror&quot; (I'm <u>not</u> advocating for The Thing), some levels of &quot;what the fuck&quot; would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like to be able to make an Angler-Fish trapper that, while in DBT, can shoot octopus tentacles out of his stomach-mounted Hideous Maw to grapple and reel in his opponents, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be more Chimera than hybrid body rearrangement.<br /> <br /> Angler Fish with Octopus Traits grafted on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:36:41-08:00","id":421988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421971#post421971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed.<br /> <br /> Also, for the record, I'm not <i>against</i> charms like Hide-Toughening Essence, it should definitely be an option, because sometimes you're a cat that's getting stomped and need to survive <i>without</i> drawing attention to the fact that you're a body-snatching abomination, or whatnot.<br /> <br /> But I'm in it for the cannibalistic shape-stealing horrors that stalk the outskirts of the town at night, so while I wouldn't describe it as &quot;body horror&quot; (I'm <u>not</u> advocating for The Thing), some levels of &quot;what the fuck&quot; would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like to be able to make an Angler-Fish trapper that, while in DBT, can shoot octopus tentacles out of his stomach-mounted Hideous Maw to grapple and reel in his opponents, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want Snake Head Defense, which turns my hair into snakes when enemies get too close... or makes rats swarm out of my shadow, or bees fly out of my sleeves, or my sleeves themselves turn into the beating, arm-breaking wings of a crane...<br /> <br /> But this is a very transitional transformation, which ends as soon as the enemy withdraws. It's the sort of thing that works regardless of my form, and thus doesn't impinge on the uniqueness of the forms I wear. Especially since it can take various forms itself, and thus be coordinated with the shape I wear.<br /> <br /> If I don't want my lion's mane to turn into snakes, then I go with the shadow-rats. If I'm already a crane, perhaps I shed feathers that become a flock of vicious bluejays.<br /> <br /> If Snake Head Defense can be upgraded to enable grapples, then it becomes the Charm that both of us want, since it would let you shoot those octopus tentacles out at any valid target within range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:37:40-08:00","id":421991,"title":"","content":"I want social applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:38:19-08:00","id":421992,"title":"","content":"I am reposting this from the Ask Dev's one question thread, hoping to move the conversation here <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407785-if-you-can-ask-the-dev-s-one-question?p=421855#post421855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hide-Toughening Essence is the Lunar taking his flesh and making it harder. Claws of the Silver Moon is taking his natural weaponry and making them more vicious. Flowing Body Evasion is taking his body and making it more graceful, flexible, agile. In all ways, the Lunar is strengthening his raw power rather than amplifying the skillful results, as a Solar would.</div> </div> </div> </div> And if it's glowy and magical but has no physical change, then it is not shapeshifting, not physical, not visceral, and as it is none of the three, it is not lunar.<br /> <br /> claws of the Silver Moon should have a physical effect-you hands should well twist into claws, or the natural weapons of your animal form should be noticeably more viscous-a tiger's claws become longer, a squid's tentacles longer and with sharp barbs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is more implied by how boring animal shape shifting becomes when you can always slap wings, fire-breathing and armor on whatever shape you happen to be wearing right now, as opposed to needing to shapeshift consecutively into something with wings, something with fire breath, and something with armor, or at least one creature which is supposed to already have all three. </div> </div> </div> Chimera Exist. Chimera are combinations of traits from various animals. Theoretically, a Lunar would become a Chimera by grafting parts from one animal onto their spirit shape. beign able to temporarily manifest parts from an animal in human form or in the form of an other animal would be a logical prerequisite to such permanent alterations to the spirit shape.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the ability to do mix and match parts could be an option chimera could have but other lunars do not, derived from their already mix and match spirit totem.<br /> <br /> I see no reason to drop such a thematic abillity-&quot;manifest animal derived mutations&quot; just because full changing ids going to be better. Especially since Lunars are supposed to be the most versatile Exalts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't see a strong need for the ability to manifest your totem's bear claws in your human form when you could just use your Deadly Bearman Transformation. Or Claws of the Silver Moon. Possibly a Tiger Style martial arts Charm, if claw-strikes in human form is very important to your character's image. </div> </div> </div>Deadly beast man should be a broadsword, not a scalpel-turning into a hulking man-beast is really the kind of thing that's only good in a situation that requires physical action and and does not require subtlety.<br /> <br /> turning into a bear to get claws is also the kind of thing that will screw you if you need to be subtle.<br /> <br /> One option to manifest animal mutations offers option to have claws while maintaining subtlety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:44:25-08:00","id":422002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421991#post421991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want social applications.</div> </div> </div> </div>...For what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:51:13-08:00","id":422030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421992#post421992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it's glowy and magical but has no physical change, then it is not shapeshifting, not physical, not visceral, and as it is none of the three, it is not lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, Lunars shouldn't have (Circle) Circle Sorcery Charms.<br /> <br /> You also run out of Strength Charm concepts FAST, because Hatewheel is ripping the rubberman out of the Lunars. You're not going to see Lunar Strength Charms enhancing punches with Luffy D. Monkey's &quot;giant fist&quot; or &quot;extending arm&quot; attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chimera Exist. Chimera are combinations of traits from various animals. </div> </div> </div>Chimera are Lunars who did something to their Totems, and thus their Spirit Shapes and Warforms.<br /> <br /> Maybe that means a Wolf-Totem Lunar added wings, fire-breathing and armor to his wolf form, but I bet it also means that these are permanent features of his wolf form from now on, and NOT features that he can just add willy-nilly to any of his other forms.<br /> <br /> So, the existence of Chimerae doesn't impact my Anti-&quot;Hybrid Body Rearrangement&quot; stance at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deadly beast man should be a broadsword, not a scalpel </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that doesn't mean that HBR is a scalpel that Lunars should get, and there are other scalpels available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:55:55-08:00","id":422051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422002#post422002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...For what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird shapeshifting/&quot;physicality&quot; Charm shit, presumably.<br /> <br /> Or for Snake Head Defense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:59:21-08:00","id":422053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421986#post421986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be more Chimera than hybrid body rearrangement.<br /> <br /> Angler Fish with Octopus Traits grafted on.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, I'd <i>also</i> like it if &quot;chimera&quot; was a social label and not a specific mechanically-defined state, similar in connotation to something like &quot;cannibal&quot;.<br /> I'm not necessarily saying it should be trivial though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421988#post421988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Snake Head Defense, which turns my hair into snakes when enemies get too close... or makes rats swarm out of my shadow, or bees fly out of my sleeves, or my sleeves themselves turn into the beating, arm-breaking wings of a crane...<br /> <br /> But this is a very transitional transformation, which ends as soon as the enemy withdraws. It's the sort of thing that works regardless of my form, and thus <b>doesn't impinge on the uniqueness of the forms I wear.</b> Especially since it can take various forms itself, and thus be coordinated with the shape I wear.<br /> <br /> If I don't want my lion's mane to turn into snakes, then I go with the shadow-rats. If I'm already a crane, perhaps I shed feathers that become a flock of vicious bluejays.<br /> <br /> If Snake Head Defense can be upgraded to enable grapples, then it becomes the Charm that both of us want, since it would let you shoot those octopus tentacles out at any valid target within range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, because i want to address it in particular (I basically agree with everything else, I like Snake-Head Defence a lot). That's valid, but I also think it's valid to want charms that <i>do</i> impinge on the forms you wear, whether it's by summoning traits of other animals in your heart's blood, or through emulation of animal traits without having their blood. Though I wouldn't go with Armor-Forming mainly because it's very generic (unless you fluff it as Dragon or Tyrant Lizard scales).<br /> <br /> I understand the concern that animal forms might get washed/drowned out with all the things packed onto them, and I don't really have an answer for that (yet) other than &quot;but what if that's what you want?&quot;<br /> I'm not saying it should be <i>catered</i> to, but shouldn't it at least be an option? What if you want to play a character that can become <a href=\"http://monsterhunter.wikia.com/wiki/Zinogre\" target=\"_blank\">Zinogre</a> (a cat-like wyvern, a God-Beast in Monster Hunter lore)?<br /> Unfortunately, I get the feeling that this is an ideological difference rooted in our separate ideas on the nature of Lunars, so I'm not sure we'll really get anywhere by debating it since it seems like we're both set pretty hard in our ideals.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure how to reconcile that with this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let Heart's Blood shapeshifting handle Lunar shapeshifting. Let the legendary power come from the Charms. Say &quot;No&quot; to Hybrid Body Rearrangement, Armor-Forming Technique and Flying Squirrel Method. </div> </div> </div>because Snake-Head Defence <i>is</i> charm-shapeshifting... I'm guessing that its temporary nature offsets that, but why is that different for Hybrid Body Rearrangement?<br /> Is it because SHD is goal-focused while HBR is an all-purpose &quot;have this for a while&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-27-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:14:12-08:00","id":422080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422030#post422030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that logic, Lunars shouldn't have (Circle) Circle Sorcery Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div> socerous initiation is like martial arts-everybody can learn it and it's intentionally out of theme for most splats.<br /> <br /> A Splat's native harms, however, should not deviate from the charms themes. if lunar themes include &quot;shapeshifting and physicality&quot; as themes, but the majority of their charms are not shapeshifting or physical, then the majority of lunar charms are not within lunar themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chimera are Lunars who did something to their Totems, and thus their Spirit Shapes and Warforms.<br /> <br /> Maybe that means a Wolf-Totem Lunar added wings, fire-breathing and armor to his wolf form, but I bet it also means that these are permanent features of his wolf form from now on, and NOT features that he can just add willy-nilly to any of his other forms.<br /> <br /> So, the existence of Chimerae doesn't impact my Anti-&quot;Hybrid Body Rearrangement&quot; stance at all. </div> </div> </div> So you don't think that being able temporarily manifest wings, armor, and fire breath should be a prerequisite to permanently grafting those traits onto the animal shape that is the reflection of your soul?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but that doesn't mean that HBR is a scalpel that Lunars should get, and there are other scalpels available. </div> </div> </div> No, but it is a scalpel that should be available for lunars that want it.;<br /> <br /> And you ignored my other points entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:19:01-08:00","id":422084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422080#post422080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Splat's native harms, however, should not deviate from the charms themes. if lunar themes include &quot;shapeshifting and physicality&quot; as themes, but the majority of their charms are not shapeshifting or physical, then the majority of lunar charms are not within lunar themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree, with one caveat: we don't know that those are the <i>only</i> themes.<br /> I'm still hoping for madness, dreams, lunacy, altered states of consciousness and intuition, personally.<br /> <br /> Edit: especially when it comes to social and mental Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:27:04-08:00","id":422148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422084#post422084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly agree, with one caveat: we don't know that those are the <i>only</i> themes.<br /> I'm still hoping for madness, dreams, lunacy, altered states of consciousness and intuition, personally.<br /> <br /> Edit: especially when it comes to social and mental Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:06:39-08:00","id":422277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421853#post421853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I've mentioned Charm-share 3 times in the last month. Has any of those times caused you grievous injury or harm?<br /> Hell I'm not even going on about it, It's a passing remark in a sentence that's wholly <i>not about it</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> So? Sexism hasn't ruined my life (or any of my games) in any way, that doesn't prevent me from personally wanting it to go.<br /> The &quot;it doesn't affect you&quot; argument isn't a valid one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're comparing 'boring/useless charm' to 'actively detrimental behavior' and calling them even? &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:28:50-08:00","id":422297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422277#post422277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're comparing 'boring/useless charm' to 'actively detrimental behavior' and calling them even? &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you see me making an equivalency? It was a criticism of the style of rhetoric. &quot;X hasn't ruined your Y&quot; doesn't preclude me from wanting X to change, especially when considering the repercussions X had and continues to have.<br /> <br /> But since that conversation is over, how'bout those Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-27-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T23:46:27-08:00","id":422661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=421992#post421992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am reposting this from the Ask Dev's one question thread, hoping to move the conversation here <hr /> And if it's glowy and magical but has no physical change, then it is not shapeshifting, not physical, not visceral, and as it is none of the three, it is not lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a foolishly narrow interpretation. Metaphor and generic magic are things which exist.<br /> <br /> Socialize is a Fire-Aspected ability for Terrestrials, but we can expect that not all socialize charms will involve something literally bursting into flame. Death and decay are in theme for Abysalls, but we can expect that not all Abyssal Charms necessarily involve someone dieing. Sidereal themes have always been notoriously esoteric, but in every edition they've had access to a certain degree of 'generic power-up magic'.<br /> <br /> It's wrong to imagine that things which are common and characteristic of a group (they do this a lot!) are strictily defining that group (They do this, and this only!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","user":"SuddenThunder","date":".  My kingdom for spellcheck on the forums ... 02-28-2015, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T03:20:32-08:00","id":422787,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of a wide, generally applicable charms and abilities, with a few areas of expertise. When Luna, the Impossible made Possible, is your divine patron and it is Her? essence powering your exaltation, the phrase &quot;I can't/don't do X.&quot; has no place being in your vocabulary. Plus, previous fluff has the Lunars being the partners and assistants of Solars, whnich presumes that Lunars used their gifts to cover areas where their respective Solars did not focus.<br /> <br /> I know the &quot;silver solars&quot; concept gets a lot of flak, but when solars, dragonblooded and even sidereals (to a point) have tools for nearly any situation and can be pretty much anything in concept, a limited toolset for Lunars won't do justice to the theme. They may not be the most powerful or cost-efficient tools, but they should be there for those who want them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 02-28-2015, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T05:52:10-08:00","id":422838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422661#post422661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a foolishly narrow interpretation. Metaphor and generic magic are things which exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Sunder is arguing that the <b>majority</b> of Lunar charms should not incorporate Shapeshifting, and should not be physical.. If the majority of charms do not apply to Lunar themes at all, then the majority of lunar charms are out of theme.<br /> <br /> There is no meaningful difference between &quot;I glow gold and become magically better at punching&quot; and &quot;I glow silver and become magically stronger, thus making my punches better&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T06:06:11-08:00","id":422843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422838#post422838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no meaningful difference between &quot;I glow gold and become magically better at punching&quot; and &quot;I glow silver and become magically stronger, thus making my punches better&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because you don't see something doesn't mean it doesn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T06:56:26-08:00","id":422872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422843#post422843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you don't see something doesn't mean it doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the meaningful difference between &quot;glow gold and punch better&quot; and &quot;glow silver and punch harder&quot;? Honest question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:09:51-08:00","id":422878,"title":"","content":"There's a world of difference between hitting harder and hitting better - watch some MMA videos if you don't believe me. A harder hit will probably be more likely to stun or even kill if it lands in a half-decent spot, but a precise enough strike can incapacitate with a tenth or even a hundredth the force. A harder hit will probably power through the opponent's defense to damage them anyway, but a &quot;better&quot; one will waste far less energy to the same effect. <br /> <br /> The primary (but far from only!) difference between &quot;punch harder&quot; and &quot;punch better&quot; is that of economy - the Solar can do what the Lunar can, more cheaply, or exert himself similarly to greater effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-28-2015, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:36:08-08:00","id":422899,"title":"","content":"I think there's some confusion here. My fault, I should have been more clear.<br /> <br /> The Solar's martial arts charms(or brawl) boil down to &quot;spend essence, glow gold if peripheral, punch/kick with magically boosted skill&quot;<br /> <br /> In the model Sunder Proposed, the equivalent Lunar charms would be in strength or dexterity, and would be &quot;spend essence, glow silver if peripheral, and magically hit harder/faster without extra exertion(unless you count the expenditure of essence as exertion)&quot;<br /> <br /> What's the difference now?<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing any meaningful difference between &quot;magically better at punching&quot; and &quot;can punch harder because magically super strong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Particularly jarring, is that the model suggests that most Lunar charms should be glowy and magical, instead of physical and visceral. Yeah, a generic super strength charm should be present, but it shouldn't be the be all end all.<br /> <br /> It should be &quot;Excellency-Stronger/more efficient but specialized boost-actual physical change(bulging muscles-sharper more vicious nat weapons)-drastic physical change drawing on some totemic representation of something something lost my train of thought.<br /> <br /> social charms should be &quot;reading the other guy's reactions and then subtle shape shifting to be better looking for whatever you're trying to do+pheromones+hypnotic eyes and the like)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 02-28-2015, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:12:20-08:00","id":423124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422838#post422838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Sunder is arguing that the <b>majority</b> of Lunar charms should not incorporate Shapeshifting, and should not be physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they shouldn't be physical. A Charm doesn't need to reshape the Lunar's body to be physical.<br /> <br /> Hide-Toughening Essence has generally never involved a silver glow, in the same way that most Solar Resistance soak Charms never invoked a golden glow. It's just that if they did have a visual effect, it would probably be silver or golden.<br /> <br /> Hide-Toughening Essence is the Lunar's skill at making his body tougher; at becoming the Nemean Anything, whether lion or tiger or bearman. Or even human. Whereas the Solar probably approaches the result through breath-control, pain-tolerance, and transcendent understanding of his own personal biology and Essence flows, the Lunar simply makes his flesh superhuman directly. By comparison, the Lunar skips across the Solar's effort to arrive at the goal.<br /> <br /> Becoming a legendary beast regardless of the specific species is well-within Lunar themes.<br /> <br /> We've been told that their Heart's Blood powers are unlikely to let them take any of the supernatural powers of gods and demons, but it still allows Lunars to alter their forms for power. It lets them run like the leopard, fly like the eagle, dive like the whale.<br /> <br /> So why shouldn't Lunar Charms eschew changing the Lunar's form and instead concentrate on giving them supernatural power equal to that of gods and demons?<br /> <br /> Both powers will each cover one half of the equation. Neither power will make the other seem redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:35:04-08:00","id":423144,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to my understanding, Rater, Lunars won't be defined by the theme of shapeshifting, but will have a central theme, and one of the methods of exploring that theme is shapeshifting. I prefer that.<br /> <br /> As for the difference between &quot;punching better because you're a better puncher&quot; and &quot;punching better because you're more physically gifted,&quot; the obvious difference is that there's basically no real difference in the punch - the practical outcome of the punch is largely determined by how much force you can transfer to the other guy, by whatever method. However, being physically gifted is more broadly applicable than to just punching.<br /> <br /> I really like Sunder the Gold's take, though the complimentary nature of the two types of abilities could be played up more. Used in conjunction, shapeshifting and Charms should be amazing. Of the two, though, I feel like Charms should be the more central to the experience of being a Lunar. I could see playing a Lunar without focusing on shapeshifting, but a Lunar with no Charms? No, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:20:32-08:00","id":423293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423144#post423144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Sunder the Gold's take, though the complimentary nature of the two types of abilities could be played up more. Used in conjunction, shapeshifting and Charms should be amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Armor-Forming Technique or Scales of the Celestial Dragon making a reappearance as an upgrade to Hide-Toughening Essence. Where HTE improves your basic soak, AFT or Scales would improve any natural armor of the Lunar's current form.<br /> <br /> Like, if I gain +1 Lethal soak from a wolf's thick fur, then this upgrade would double it. (Any doubling would be capped by the Lunar's Essence or something, to keep it from getting crazy.)<br /> <br /> The same or similar upgrade might improve the Lunar's manufactured armor, assuming it's attuned to him or otherwise made to count as part of him enough for the internal bent of Lunar magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:30:09-08:00","id":423308,"title":"","content":"That's how I always saw their Excellencies working, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:36:54-08:00","id":423319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423124#post423124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say they shouldn't be physical. A Charm doesn't need to reshape the Lunar's body to be physical.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're exact words were magical and glowing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Magical and glowing&quot; means &quot;no physical change&quot; means not physical means not Lunar, based on what the Devs told us about how Lunars work<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hide-Toughening Essence has generally never involved a silver glow, in the same way that most Solar Resistance soak Charms never invoked a golden glow. It's just that if they did have a visual effect, it would probably be silver or golden. </div> </div> </div> Hide Toughing Essence should have the physical effect of the Lunars hide toughing. if a visual effect i s eeded, then the hide being noticibly toughed, such as with corocodile scales or a thick pelt o chitinous shell manifesting itself, should be the visual effect, becuase lunars are physical, visceral, shape shifters, not magic silver glowy people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Becoming a legendary beast regardless of the specific species is well-within Lunar themes. </div> </div> </div> and legendary beasts have legendary features-legendary claws, legendary size. &quot;super strength with no physical change&quot; is an excellency, not a legendary feature.<br /> <br /> [quote]We've been told that their Heart's Blood powers are unlikely to let them take any of the supernatural powers of gods and demons[quote] This is irrelevant to the discussion.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it still allows Lunars to alter their forms for power. It lets them run like the leopard, fly like the eagle, dive like the whale. </div> </div> </div> Wrong, the devs said that Lunar charms made you &quot;Smart <b>like</b> the Elephant, not smart <b>as</b> an elephant&quot; You don't turn into an eagle to fly <b>like</b> the eagle, you turn into an eagle to fly <b>as</b> an eagle<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why shouldn't Lunar Charms eschew changing the Lunar's form and instead concentrate on giving them supernatural power equal to that of gods and demons? </div> </div> </div>Because the two are not mutually exclusive? Because Knacks are no longer a thing and shapeshifting is being integrated into the charm set, meaning that distinguishing between shapeshifting and charms has no point becuase beyond the most minor shifting, there is no distinction at all? Because Lunar Thematics are Physical and Visceral Shapeshifters who &quot;shape themselves and perceptions of themselves&quot;, meaning from that that most lunar powers should involve shaping oneself or shaping how others see you in a way that does not include illusions, as illusions are not in theme for lunars, and that the three lunar castes are, currently, &quot;Hunter, Trickster, Shaman&quot; with only the shaman possibly letting &quot;alter your attributes without altering your body&quot; being in theme, but I doubt it again, because improving ones attributed without altering their body is neither shaping themselves nor shaping a perception of themselves.<br /> <br /> if you're entire splat is &quot;up your powers ina way that is not physical, due to being magical and 'glowy'&quot; with no physical change, then you're entire splat's charm set is limited to &quot;generic super strength, generic super toughness, generic super speed, generic super intelligence, generic super not needing sleepness, generic not getting sickness, and generic hot as hellness&quot; oh, and you can also turn into animals.<br /> <br /> Basically, lunars would only have basic heart's blood and generic powers, and then they'd be bland and boring compared to &quot;near perfect disguises due to shapeshifting, getting other people to do what you want with pheromones, being immune poison, being able to twist your hands into vicious claws and bulge up your muscles to tear someones head off&quot; and all of the other physical and vsisceral(not to mention in theme, unlike what you're suggesting) powers that are more flavorful than &quot;silver solar that punches harder instead of better&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 02-28-2015, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:42:36-08:00","id":423324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423319#post423319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becuase Knacks are no longer athing and shapeshifting is being intergrated into the charm set?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we got any official word on that. If you got that idea from me, I was just stating my preference - which I think is a logical extrapolation of the way Eclipses changed - and wasn't going by any info we actually have about them.<br /> <br /> If we did get info, then I'm not aware of it and would love to be corrected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-28-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:47:40-08:00","id":423327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=422053#post422053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because Snake-Head Defence <i>is</i> charm-shapeshifting... I'm guessing that its temporary nature offsets that, but why is that different for Hybrid Body Rearrangement?<br /> <br /> Is it because SHD is goal-focused while HBR is an all-purpose &quot;have this for a while&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>That may very well be!<br /> <br /> Snake Head Defense as I envision it is very goal/effect oriented; it creates an environmental hazard for any enemies who get too close to you, but the specific form the hazard takes (while always bestial) isn't important. Because it's not important, it can be fluffed as anything appropriate (or alien) to your form.<br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Rearrangement focuses more on the means; you increase soak by growing armor, you fly by growing wings, you strike more often by growing arms. It places the emphasis on the form it provides, which detracts from the importance of the form you are wearing.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Hybrid Body Rearrangement is a toolkit Charm that steals focus from other Charms.<br /> <br /> We've already mentioned Armor-Forming Technique as an alternative to HBR's ability to grow armor. That effect is ALL Armor-Forming Technique does.<br /> <br /> Let us say that Lunars have a Charm that allow them to fly without wings, by standing and running on thin air or something. That's ALL the Charm does.<br /> <br /> Snake Head Defense only surrounds the Lunar with a protective hazard, and doesn't do anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> You could use forms that fly, forms that bear natural armor, or forms that have natural protective hazards (always-on-fire, electrified, clinging vapors of poisonous breath)... But the Charms are enhancing these forms, rather than making them something they're not.<br /> <br /> That's how it feels to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:52:39-08:00","id":423332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423144#post423144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Sunder the Gold's take, though the complimentary nature of the two types of abilities could be played up more. Used in conjunction, shapeshifting and Charms should be amazing. Of the two, though, I feel like Charms should be the more central to the experience of being a Lunar. I could see playing a Lunar without focusing on shapeshifting, but a Lunar with no Charms? No, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, devs have already said that if you don't want to play a shapeshifter, you should play something other than a lunar(and avoid a couple other splats, too.)<br /> <br /> And &quot;Physicality&quot; and &quot;Shapeshifting&quot; are two of the Lunar Themes, the ones that seem pretty important to how they work, since Lunars &quot;shape themselves and perceptions of themselves&quot;<br /> <br /> And &quot;be stronger without any physical changes&quot; is not physicality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:57:04-08:00","id":423336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423332#post423332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And &quot;Physicality&quot; and &quot;Shapeshifting&quot; are two of the Lunar Themes-</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does that work for Mental or Social attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:03:24-08:00","id":423344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423327#post423327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hybrid Body Rearrangement focuses more on the means; you increase soak by growing armor, you fly by growing wings, you strike more often by growing arms. It places the emphasis on the form it provides, which detracts from the importance of the form you are wearing.</div> </div> </div> </div> All of which is a natural extension of Lunar themes-that they are &quot;Physical&quot; shifters who alter &quot;Themselves and perceptions of themselves&quot;<br /> <br /> being stronger with no physical change in neither<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the fact that Hybrid Body Rearrangement is a toolkit Charm that steals focus from other Charms. </div> </div> </div> Citation needed. A tool kit charm can only improve other charms-Hybrid Body combined with Armor-forming technique to make <b>Better </b>natural armor than the set either would give you on your own, or use hybrid body to grow bear claws and then use Claws of the Silver Moon to twist them into truly formidable and vicious natural weapons.<br /> <br /> I also note that the existence of Armor Forming technique would contradict your stance, that lunar charms should be neither shapeshifting nor physical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've already mentioned Armor-Forming Technique as an alternative to HBR's ability to grow armor. That effect is ALL Armor-Forming Technique does. </div> </div> </div> see above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let us say that Lunars have a Charm that allow them to fly without wings, by standing and running on thin air or something. That's ALL the Charm does. </div> </div> </div> Out of theme-it does not change the lunars body, does not alter ones perception of a lunar, and is not physically<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Snake Head Defense only surrounds the Lunar with a protective hazard, and doesn't do anything else. </div> </div> </div> and is something that can not be replicated by or augmented with Hybrid Body Rearrangement.<br /> <br /> And is also a shape shifting power, and thus Lunars should not have it, by your argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could use forms that fly, forms that bear natural armor, or forms that have natural protective hazards (always-on-fire, electrified, clinging vapors of poisonous breath)... But the Charms are enhancing these forms, rather than making them something they're not.<br /> <br /> That's how it feels to me. </div> </div> </div>Or you could take those traits, and manifest mutations derived from them in your other forms in order to use a fraction of their power whenever you need to, because Lunars are the versatile splat, and having to turn into a hulking man beast or a bear to use claws is a lack of versatility.<br /> <br /> versatility is having a bunch of things you can do, and a bunch of ways to do them-four different ways to have claws, some better to use in certain situations than others, that can be combined if needed, that's versatile.<br /> <br /> Apply that to any and every physical change the lunar might need to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 02-28-2015, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:10:26-08:00","id":423350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423336#post423336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how does that work for Mental or Social attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say for mental attributes, since I'm not sure what each one does, but for social it's &quot;subtle shapeshifting to make yourself look more appropriate for whatever you're trying to do(more attractive for seduction, more fearsome for intimidation, more regal when commanding, more trustworthy when lying) and pheremones, and shapeshifting into near perfect disguises, thus greatly lowering the number of success needed on a larceny roll to pass yourself off as someone else, and the like&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:06:40-08:00","id":423482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423344#post423344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All of which is a natural extension of Lunar themes-that they are &quot;Physical&quot; shifters who alter &quot;Themselves and perceptions of themselves&quot;<br /> <br /> being stronger with no physical change in neither</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, how direct does the link have to be? For example, a sort of &quot;totemic&quot; transformation where the anima flashes with the shape of a Tyrant lizard and the exalt becomes as strong as a TL without physically turning into one would still be thematic imo. There is a change on some level.even if the cosmetic appearance does not change.<br /> <br /> And frankly, I get the idea that shapeshifting is a typical lunar thing and sort of their unique gimmick but the idea that Lunars can ONLY do things through shapeshifting... eh that seems a bit narrow for a major exalted type.We'll see how it ends up working, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 02-28-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:29:17-08:00","id":423541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423482#post423482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, how direct does the link have to be? For example, a sort of &quot;totemic&quot; transformation where the anima flashes with the shape of a Tyrant lizard and the exalt becomes as strong as a TL without physically turning into one would still be thematic imo. There is a change on some level.even if the cosmetic appearance does not change.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be pointless. You don't to Lunars for morphic resonance. You go to them for straight-up changing your form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And frankly, I get the idea that shapeshifting is a typical lunar thing and sort of their unique gimmick but the idea that Lunars can ONLY do things through shapeshifting... eh that seems a bit narrow for a major exalted type.We'll see how it ends up working, I guess. </div> </div> </div>The core concept of &quot;Lunar Exalted&quot; is &quot;animalistic shapeshifters&quot;, and this should never be in a place where it can be put completely out of view and forgotten, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:36:43-08:00","id":423545,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/262\" target=\"_blank\">A relevant quote:</a><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not trying to model the Hulk with Lunars, though there are some things about the Hulk that I admire.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mystique is the best Lunar inspiration. I saw her quite a bit but never knew much about her. From what I saw, she was a conniving coward and a psychologically abusive mother. If shapeshifting is all it takes to make you a Lunar, so is the T-1000 and that guy from Deep Space Nine.<br /> <br /> <b>I don't plan on turning Lunars into the Animal Exalted</b>, because there are a few problems with that premise:<br /> <br /> 1) Animal powers using animal logic go in a Sci-Fi direction, unfitting for a mythology world.<br /> 2) Animal powers being the source of your awesome power makes you feel like the Chosen of Zoo Tycoon.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we get rid of the spirit shape or animal associations for some of their magic. That does mean that we probably don't want their Charm set being modeled in its entirety after Things Animals Do\u00e2\u201e\u00a2. A mythic association is cool here and there (Graceful Crane Stance, Ten Ox Meditation), but when my greatest intelligence Charm is based on an elephant or a dolphin I start to feel like a monkey, and the whole Charm set starts to look like Jump the Shark Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal powers here and there: Yes.<br /> All of Lunars revolving around animal themes and animal transformations: No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:47:13-08:00","id":423559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423541#post423541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be pointless. You don't to Lunars for morphic resonance. You go to them for straight-up changing your form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? First, the connection that fuels the transformation can be more than skin deep. There is a mystical link underneath the flesh reconstruction. Second,if I can change my form, then it should be fully possible to change how something works AND determine how it looks.It can be a twofold transformation, so to speak, Plus, who else has a better claim on such a feat? You are swelling with raw power and a Solar, as far as I can tell, is about skill, not so much raw strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423541#post423541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core concept of &quot;Lunar Exalted&quot; is &quot;animalistic shapeshifters&quot;, and this should never be in a place where it can be put completely out of view and forgotten, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not disagree it is a core concept, but I disagree that it is how <b>everything</b> should be done. As an example, to me, the core concept of dragon-blooded are &quot;elemental-themed dynasties&quot;, but that does not mean all their charms have to do with some energy discharges, growing flowers and so on. The connection to the element is always there, but it is sometimes metaphorical, - fire is tied to passion, wood and life to music, air to thought and knowledge, and they had charms for all of those. Luna is tied to other things than shapeshifting - if we go by the 2E book her aspects include an explorer, a mystic, a lover, and many more. I expect Her? chosen to be just as versatile as adapting those roles as those of Sol Invistus are in developing his. I want shapeshifting to be in there, but I also want the visceral emotion, the ties to others, the strange genius. I know it is a tall order, but I am hoping we get something to do the concept justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 02-28-2015, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:01:29-08:00","id":423569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423324#post423324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we got any official word on that. If you got that idea from me, I was just stating my preference - which I think is a logical extrapolation of the way Eclipses changed - and wasn't going by any info we actually have about them.<br /> <br /> If we did get info, then I'm not aware of it and would love to be corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was that Knacks were no longer a separate Thing because there was not a reason for them to be (because blocking Eclipse Charmshare is no longer a concern).<br /> <br /> That said, they might remain as a Thing to facilitate something like a Charmcloud aspect - a shapeshifting power built on Wits that has a prerequisite built on Dex, for example, which is not the kind of thing you expect to see in a straight-Attribute Charmtree.<br /> <br /> Not that I think this would be terribly popular - it wasn't in 2e, because it established artificial competency prerequisites in Attributes other than the end-result power, which forces particular builds that may be undesired by the player (needing Manipulation 4 to get the Manipulation 4 Knack that is the prerequisite to the Wits 5 Knack, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-28-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:14:58-08:00","id":423577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423559#post423559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? First, the connection that fuels the transformation can be more than skin deep. There is a mystical link underneath the flesh reconstruction. Second,if I can change my form, then it should be fully possible to change how something works AND determine how it looks.It can be a twofold transformation, so to speak, Plus, who else has a better claim on such a feat? You are swelling with raw power and a Solar, as far as I can tell, is about skill, not so much raw strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that isn't a Lunar. They're supposed to wear obvious changes proudly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not disagree it is a core concept, but I disagree that it is how <b>everything</b> should be done. As an example, to me, the core concept of dragon-blooded are &quot;elemental-themed dynasties&quot;, but that does not mean all their charms have to do with some energy discharges, growing flowers and so on. The connection to the element is always there, but it is sometimes metaphorical, - fire is tied to passion, wood and life to music, air to thought and knowledge, and they had charms for all of those. Luna is tied to other things than shapeshifting - if we go by the 2E book her aspects include an explorer, a mystic, a lover, and many more. I expect Her? chosen to be just as versatile as adapting those roles as those of Sol Invistus are in developing his. I want shapeshifting to be in there, but I also want the visceral emotion, the ties to others, the strange genius. I know it is a tall order, but I am hoping we get something to do the concept justice. </div> </div> </div>And you don't do it by fake turning into something. That takes away from a large measure of visceral impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:24:34-08:00","id":423586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423545#post423545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/262\" target=\"_blank\">A relevant quote:</a><br /> <br /> Animal powers here and there: Yes.<br /> All of Lunars revolving around animal themes and animal transformations: No.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, Morke disavowed that quote not long ago in RPG.net. Lunars are more tied than animals now than in the time of that quote.<br /> <br /> (But I doubt they will be only all-animal, all-the-time, even if that is their main focus.)<br /> <br /> Also, I have to say: I always HATED the nomenclature 'Knacks'. Of all things you could name miracles of shapeshifting... 'Knacks' sounded so boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:35:26-08:00","id":423618,"title":"","content":"I liked &quot;Knacks&quot;. Made me think of a tricksters tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:38:53-08:00","id":423621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423586#post423586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, Morke disavowed that quote not long ago in RPG.net. Lunars are more tied than animals now than in the time of that quote.<br /> <br /> (But I doubt they will be only all-animal, all-the-time, even if that is their main focus.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So we WILL be playing Chosen Of Zoo Tycoon then?<br /> <br /> Dang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:39:34-08:00","id":423622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423344#post423344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Citation needed. A tool kit charm can only improve other charms</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a toolkit Charm is a Charm that does far too much. A Charm is supposed to be just one tool; perhaps a tool with many applications, but not a whole box of tools.<br /> <br /> I meant to explain this in my post, but it seems that sentence fell out of my head! Embarassing.<br /> <br /> But a Lunar shouldn't ever need HBR. He can turn into something with claws and use Claws of the Silver Moon to make those claws deadlier, or he can use the Charm in human form to treat his fingers as claws or his bare knuckles as deadly weapons.<br /> <br /> The Lunar becomes a legendary wild man, or a legendary werebeast, or a legendary beast. His shapeshifting determines the form, and his Charms provide the &quot;legendary&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:46:03-08:00","id":423626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423621#post423621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we WILL be playing Chosen Of Zoo Tycoon then?<br /> <br /> Dang.</div> </div> </div> </div>If animals are as cool as the T. Lizard preview implied, what do you see as the problem here?<br /> <br /> I for one am excited to finally have functional Beast Boy/Vixen in combat. But I do see how extrapolating that to socials/mentals is hard or weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:50:25-08:00","id":423630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423626#post423626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If animals are as cool as the T. Lizard preview implied, what do you see as the problem here?<br /> <br /> I for one am excited to finally have functional Beast Boy/Vixen in combat. But I do see how extrapolating that to socials/mentals is hard or weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you typically don't turn into a turtle to seduce someone.<br /> <br /> There's Heart's Blood (the turtle) and there's Charms, and Charms are generally where you find Lunar super-seduction. Though one shouldn't discount the advantage of wearing the face of your mark's &quot;type&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:09:43-08:00","id":423646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423630#post423630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you typically don't turn into a turtle to seduce someone.<br /> <br /> There's Heart's Blood (the turtle) and there's Charms, and Charms are generally where you find Lunar super-seduction. Though one shouldn't discount the advantage of wearing the face of your mark's &quot;type&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess to me it's still unclear how the non-physical Charms are going to be portrayed fluff-wise, if Lunars are much more explicitly the Animal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:40:34-08:00","id":423670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423646#post423646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess to me it's still unclear how the non-physical Charms are going to be portrayed fluff-wise, if Lunars are much more explicitly the Animal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Smart LIKE a fox&quot; rather than &quot;smart AS a fox&quot;, is how Morke put it.<br /> <br /> Lunar Charms will evoke godlike beasts. Not a coyote, but Coyote. Not a rabbit, but <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">El-Ahrairah, The Prince of a Thousand Enemies.<br /> <br /> If Hide-Toughening Essence is &quot;I'm tough like Father Rhino&quot;, then a social Charm might be &quot;I'm as coy as Madame Butterfly&quot;.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:42:24-08:00","id":423718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423344#post423344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All of which is a natural extension of Lunar themes-that they are &quot;Physical&quot; shifters who alter &quot;Themselves and perceptions of themselves&quot;<br /> <br /> being stronger with no physical change in neither</div> </div> </div> </div>I use Hide-Toughening Essence in human form to take a hit from some predator without flinching then use Claws of the Silver Moon to rip its throat out. I do this in front of a group of people, I've most likely altered their perception of me by being stronger without physical changes to myself.<br /> <br /> I use essence to make myself tough like a rhino sounds Physical enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:45:00-08:00","id":423721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423630#post423630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you typically don't turn into a turtle to seduce someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Otohime might disagree on that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">...a social Charm might be &quot;I'm as coy as Madame Butterfly&quot;.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I think that you picked a bad example name here.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:49:22-08:00","id":423723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423721#post423721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otohime might disagree on that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not familiar enough with that myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that you picked a bad example name here.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR] </div> </div> </div>As charming as Lord Peacock, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"