ory/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423767#post423767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daughter of the Dragon King of the Sea, got caught as a turtle on shore, helped out by a guy named Urashima. Of course, things start to go a bit fae when he visits the Dragons' abode.</div> </div> </div> </div>The TURTLE was the princess Oto? Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T21:50:46-08:00","id":423816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423794#post423794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TURTLE was the princess Oto? Huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes. It depends on who's telling the story.<br /> <br /> Perhaps less in flux, the story of the Grateful Crane/Crane Wife, where a childless couple or a youth comes upon an injured animal, provides aid, and finds out that they have a mysterious new roommate or surrogate child the next day,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-01-2015, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:12:47-08:00","id":424058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423545#post423545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/262\" target=\"_blank\">A relevant quote:</a><br /> <br /> Animal powers here and there: Yes.<br /> All of Lunars revolving around animal themes and animal transformations: No.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chosen of animals exclusively-No.<br /> <br /> Powers that must be physical <b>or </b>involve shapeshifting: Common sense indicates yes, as &quot;shapeshifters big on physicality who do things by altering themselves or perceptions of themselves&quot; would require that most of their powers involve shapeshifting or physicality. That's just basic logic.<br /> <br /> X is Y. Y requires Z. Thus, X requires Z.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing anything in this debate that would make that reasoning fallacious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:17:56-08:00","id":424060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423482#post423482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, how direct does the link have to be? For example, a sort of &quot;totemic&quot; transformation where the anima flashes with the shape of a Tyrant lizard and the exalt becomes as strong as a TL without physically turning into one would still be thematic imo. There is a change on some level.even if the cosmetic appearance does not change.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a borderline case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423482#post423482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And frankly, I get the idea that shapeshifting is a typical lunar thing and sort of their unique gimmick but the idea that Lunars can ONLY do things through shapeshifting... eh that seems a bit narrow for a major exalted type.We'll see how it ends up working, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting is very versatile power, even if rubberman and &quot;rubberman&quot; esque powers are not in theme for lunars.<br /> <br /> Also, who is saying that Lunars would have to do everything with Shapeshifting? The argument is that Sunder's view of lunar charms, that they should be raw upgrades to the Lunar's physical form but that have no physical effect on that form, does not match the stated themes of Lunars, that of being physical, visceral, animalistic shapeshifters(the animalistic part is unnecessary for this discussion)<br /> <br /> And it's not, because &quot;spend motes, be stronger with not noticeable physical changes&quot; is, at most, a Lunar excellency, not the entirety of the strength tree, because something like that is bland, boring, and limiting. And again, if it's not physical and not shapeshifting, if it's &quot;magical and glowing&quot; as Sunder put it, then it's not Lunar, because that's not what Lunars are said to be. Claws of the Silver Moon should actually involve growing claws, not just your fingernails magically becoming as hard as steel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 03-01-2015, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:29:51-08:00","id":424067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423559#post423559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not disagree it is a core concept, but I disagree that it is how <b>everything</b> should be done. As an example, to me, the core concept of dragon-blooded are &quot;elemental-themed dynasties&quot;, but that does not mean all their charms have to do with some energy discharges, growing flowers and so on. The connection to the element is always there, but it is sometimes metaphorical, - fire is tied to passion, wood and life to music, air to thought and knowledge, and they had charms for all of those. Luna is tied to other things than shapeshifting - if we go by the 2E book her aspects include an explorer, a mystic, a lover, and many more. I expect Her? chosen to be just as versatile as adapting those roles as those of Sol Invistus are in developing his. I want shapeshifting to be in there, but I also want the visceral emotion, the ties to others, the strange genius. I know it is a tall order, but I am hoping we get something to do the concept justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are the skill Exalted. They do everything with Supernatural extensions of their mundane skills.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the Fate Exalted. The Majority of their charms work by manipulating Fate.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded are the Elemental Exalted. The Majority of their powers manipulate the Elements, and the rest draw on the Elements Thematically.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are the Underworld's Skill Exalted. All of their charms are manifestations of Supernaturally enhanced mundane skill taken to logical extremes and then twisted by death, or alternatively by using Underworld/Death Lord Powers<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are the Machine Exalted. All of their Charms are machines implanted in their bodies or otherwise connected to them.<br /> <br /> What is so special about Lunars that they get to go so far beyond their own themes when getting charms when noone else does? Isn't that one of the problems Lunars had? If you put in to many charms that are not shapeshifting and not physical, than Lunar themes become diluted, and you get he Silver Solar problem again, as I've been alluding to in the &quot;magically more skilled vs Magically more powerful and how in game mechanics there's no meaningful difference between them&quot; line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:34:46-08:00","id":424069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423621#post423621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we WILL be playing Chosen Of Zoo Tycoon then?<br /> <br /> Dang.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exact words were along the lines of &quot;Not Smart as an Elephant, Smart Like an Elephant&quot; &quot;Not Strong as an Ox, but Strong Like an Ox&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:41:55-08:00","id":424077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423622#post423622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, a toolkit Charm is a Charm that does far too much. A Charm is supposed to be just one tool; perhaps a tool with many applications, but not a whole box of tools.<br /> <br /> I meant to explain this in my post, but it seems that sentence fell out of my head! Embarassing.<br /> <br /> But a Lunar shouldn't ever need HBR. He can turn into something with claws and use Claws of the Silver Moon to make those claws deadlier, or he can use the Charm in human form to treat his fingers as claws or his bare knuckles as deadly weapons.<br /> <br /> The Lunar becomes a legendary wild man, or a legendary werebeast, or a legendary beast. His shapeshifting determines the form, and his Charms provide the &quot;legendary&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> They should <b>both</b> provide the Legendary&quot; And &quot;Magical and Glowy&quot; does not provide the legendary features that legendary beasts have.<br /> <br /> And once more you ignore all of my other points. Bad form Sunder.<br /> <br /> Let me repeat. Lunars are supposed to be versatile. Versatility is having tools that can do lots of things(Like the tool kit charms you so clearly hate for no rational reason). But it's also having more than one way to do something in case one method of doing it won't work.<br /> <br /> for example, a Lunar needs to be subtle, but also needs claws. Turning into a hulkling manbeast, or a bear, or shifting your claws into your glorious but vicious Claws of the Silver Moon, none of that is subtle. This is where you use Hybrid Body Rearrangement to give yourself the &quot;claws&quot; mutation by subtly shifting your fingernails into small but sharp talon Subtle, but weaker than the other three methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:45:00-08:00","id":424078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423630#post423630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you typically don't turn into a turtle to seduce someone.<br /> <br /> There's Heart's Blood (the turtle) and there's Charms, and Charms are generally where you find Lunar super-seduction. Though one shouldn't discount the advantage of wearing the face of your mark's &quot;type&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those charms should be things like &quot;Pheromones to smell sexy&quot; or &quot;subtly alter your appearance to become closer to your Target's &quot;type&quot; as opposed to &quot;magically sexier for no reason&quot; which is, if anything, an appearance excellency. At most&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:47:32-08:00","id":424087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=423718#post423718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I use Hide-Toughening Essence in human form to take a hit from some predator without flinching then use Claws of the Silver Moon to rip its throat out. I do this in front of a group of people, I've most likely altered their perception of me by being stronger without physical changes to myself.<br /> <br /> I use essence to make myself tough like a rhino sounds Physical enough for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claws of the Silver Moon should give you the fucking claws of the silver moon.<br /> <br /> Hide Toughening Essence should give you a tougher hide.<br /> <br /> &quot;Magic and Glowy&quot; using Sunder's words, is neither a physical effect nor is it shapeshifting, and the charm didn't alter peoples perceptions, that's not part of the charm's effect, it's an incidental use and incidental uses don't count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:08:52-08:00","id":424168,"title":"","content":"Unless they have the obvious keyword and it says in the charm, &quot;Magic and glowy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:46:10-08:00","id":424190,"title":"","content":"Rater, what do you want?<br /> <br /> As a fellow Asperger, I understand where you're coming from (I spent several years in that place after the <i>First</i> Edition of Lunars was printed), but take a step back and examine this for a moment: <br /> <br /> We may be right, you may be right, but is it worth spending this much energy arguing about it? The authors have already decided what they're going to do for Lunar aesthetics. If we're right, you're not likely to convince them otherwise; you're certainly not convincing us. If you're right, you don't <i>need</i> to convince anyone.<br /> <br /> How about trying to relax and change your focus; go do something fun that isn't as frustrating?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certainly tired of trying to convince you with limited written communication and no hard evidence, where getting across the EXACT IDEA is hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:25:10-08:00","id":424212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=424190#post424190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We may be right, you may be right, but is it worth spending this much energy arguing about it? The authors have already decided what they're going to do for Lunar aesthetics. </div> </div> </div> </div>This is generally good advice to keep in mind. Yes, I may not like where things may be going (given the reactions of everyone at my table to tibdits and dev comments, there's about even chances that Lunars end up as just a primary antagonist splat at my table, Abyssal style), but it's not like obsessing over it and complaining when we don't have enough of the details to make changes and fixes is going to change much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:37:58-08:00","id":424235,"title":"","content":"I dunno about the rest of you, but I have fun at these discussions.<br /> <br /> Also, Aspy4Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:45:10-08:00","id":424264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=424190#post424190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rater, what do you want?<br /> <br /> As a fellow Asperger, I understand where you're coming from (I spent several years in that place after the <i>First</i> Edition of Lunars was printed), but take a step back and examine this for a moment:<br /> <br /> We may be right, you may be right, but is it worth spending this much energy arguing about it? The authors have already decided what they're going to do for Lunar aesthetics. If we're right, you're not likely to convince them otherwise; you're certainly not convincing us. If you're right, you don't <i>need</i> to convince anyone.<br /> <br /> How about trying to relax and change your focus; go do something fun that isn't as frustrating?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certainly tired of trying to convince you with limited written communication and no hard evidence, where getting across the EXACT IDEA is hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>You made a statement-Lunars should not have X becuase they should be Y.<br /> <br /> I provided a counter argument The Devs said that Lunars will be Z, and Y is not in theme with Z. Z also permits X. Thus, it is more likely that Lunars will have X than that they won't.<br /> <br /> You proceed to continue arguing that Lunars should not have X even though it's been disproven that Lunars should be Y because Y is not compatible with Z and Z has been confirmed to be what Lunar Powers are about.<br /> <br /> you argue that Lunar charms should not be physical,that they should, to use your own words, be &quot;magic and glowing&quot; with no noticeable physical alterations to the Lunar. This is despite the fact that Lunars are all about changing themselves and perceptions of themselves in ways that a physical and visceral, and that lunars are meant to revel in obvious physical changes.<br /> <br /> and no, I don't think that bystanders thinking you're stronger after you punch a guy to death counts ans shaping others perceptions, because you are not influencing them to perceive you in that way, it is not the only perception of you that could be derived from that act, and because that is not the intended function of the charm.<br /> <br /> I imagine that strength charms will be in the &quot;shape self&quot; category.<br /> <br /> I then provided other arguments for the support of Lunars having X-drawing on how Versatile Lunars are supposed to be, and how logical it is to have such a power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 03-01-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:15:58-08:00","id":425231,"title":"","content":"While it partakes in a childish sort of one upmanship that can't possibly be good for the game I'm none the less emotionally attached to the view of Lunar Exalted shown in panels three and four of <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0074.html\" target=\"_blank\">this comic</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:13:36-08:00","id":425380,"title":"","content":"Sigh, I really wish people would stop brining up KoC. It's dead, gone, and not coming back, and there are other comics out there that are still in progress and are more deserving of attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:58:38-08:00","id":425428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=425380#post425380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh, I really wish people would stop brining up KoC. It's dead, gone, and not coming back, and there are other comics out there that are still in progress and are more deserving of attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not dead, just sleeping. [/denial]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:10:49-08:00","id":425596,"title":"","content":"It's really sad <i>why</i> it died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:30:15-08:00","id":425610,"title":"","content":"Why did it die? Did somethign happen to the author/artist (I wasn't really following it, but it had some nice stuff in it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:46:05-08:00","id":425633,"title":"","content":"He got something wrong with his hands.<br /> <br /> Tenditis, was it?<br /> <br /> Yeah, his hands done got fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:56:43-08:00","id":425643,"title":"","content":"I believe it was tendonitis, at least as a heavy contributing factor. :/ Poor guy seemed really disappointed that he wasn't able to keep it going.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, while he's decided something as intensive as the comic is too much (at least for now), he has been able to go for some less demanding pursuits. Take a look <a href=\"http://tgchan.org/wiki/Jukashi\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for some general descriptions and links to the archives for a few quests (including the first two parts of the Exalted-oriented &quot;Lunar Quest&quot;) he's done on tgchan. They're cool reads!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:42:44-08:00","id":425737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=425380#post425380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh, I really wish people would stop brining up KoC. It's dead, gone, and not coming back, and there are other comics out there that are still in progress and are more deserving of attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>A work doesn't become less valid as an inspiration just because the author isn't writing any more of it, or else FINISHED works would cease to be valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:05:48-08:00","id":426138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=425737#post425737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A work doesn't become less valid as an inspiration just because the author isn't writing any more of it, or else FINISHED works would cease to be valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that there are other comics out there that are still being written which are more deserving of attention than a comic that has been dead for years and not coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T05:32:44-08:00","id":426470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426138#post426138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that there are other comics out there that are still being written which are more deserving of attention than a comic that has been dead for years and not coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div>IT has not been declared that it's not coming back by the artist who wrte it, he's still saying he wants to find a way to finish it.<br /> <br /> And more deserving is your opinion. it is clearly not an opinion shared by many others here, if you're complaints about how others keep brining up Keychain are anything to go by.<br /> <br /> Once more, if &quot;dead and not coming back&quot; meant something wasn't viable inspiration, then you have to toss Gilgamesh, the Greek Heroes, Norse Mythology, most ancient Chinese or Japanese Legends, and a crap ton of classic Anime down the garbage disposal along with Keychain, and then Exalted doesn't exist in the first place.<br /> <br /> You have nothing to argue with but opinions, and opinions don't win arguments.<br /> <br /> good day sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:59:25-08:00","id":426609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426470#post426470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once more, if &quot;dead and not coming back&quot; meant something wasn't viable inspiration, then you have to toss Gilgamesh, the Greek Heroes, Norse Mythology, most ancient Chinese or Japanese Legends, and a crap ton of classic Anime down the garbage disposal along with Keychain, and then Exalted doesn't exist in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you kidding with your list of examples? Look at how much of that's been rehashed or rebooted in recent years! Last year had <i>two</i> Hercules movies from two different companies! A movie based off <i>The Journey to the West</i> is on Netflix <b>right now</b>, <i>Evangelion</i> has been getting sequels and remakes and reboots since practically the day they made it, MCU's Thor has had two movies to himself, and will be in the <i>Avengers</i> sequel - fuck, even Arnold's getting off his dusty old ass to play Conan again! <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong: old, dead, or discontinued sources can still be valid inspiration, but pretty much everything on your list has persisted into the modern day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have nothing to argue with but opinions, and opinions don't win arguments. </div> </div> </div>I'll have to let Rater202 know, thanks for the tip!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">Seriously, bro? Opinions are totally important, and an impassioned argument in support of or against an opinion can totally sway other people. Hell, if so many of your posts hadn't been lost, I don't doubt I could quote quite a few where you jump to the defense of your opinions.</span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> good day sir. </div> </div> </div>To you as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-03-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:11:35-08:00","id":426618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426609#post426609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you kidding with your list of examples? Look at how much of that's been rehashed or rebooted in recent years! Last year had <i>two</i> Hercules movies from two different companies! A movie based off <i>The Journey to the West</i> is on Netflix <b>right now</b>, <i>Evangelion</i> has been getting sequels and remakes and reboots since practically the day they made it, MCU's Thor has had two movies to himself, and will be in the <i>Avengers</i> sequel - fuck, even Arnold's getting off his dusty old ass to play Conan again!</div> </div> </div> </div>But that supports what he's saying, because the old sources that these reboots are being drawn from <i>are</i> valid inspiration, despite having been &quot;finished&quot; years, decades or even centuries ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:27:10-08:00","id":426632,"title":"","content":"You misunderstand me. My point is, he can't very well give them as examples of things that are &quot;dead and not coming back&quot; because they are <i>by definition</i> <b>alive and well.</b><br /> <br /> <i>Adaptation is life.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:56:12-08:00","id":426646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426470#post426470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IT has not been declared that it's not coming back by the artist who wrte it, he's still saying he wants to find a way to finish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I've been reading webcomics since the early days of Bob and George. I have a file on my computer with links to over fifty different webcomics, all of varying styles, storylines, genres and update schedules, and roughly a third of them have stopped updated with the author saying stuff like &quot;I'd love to come back to it!&quot; or &quot;the next update is just around the corner!&quot; And you know what I've noticed? Literally (and I'm using that word in the literal sense) none of them have updated once the author stopped for a prolonged period of time. Webcomics take a lot of time and effort to work on, and once that momentum stops, it's unlikely to pick up again. I applaud the author of KoC for intending to come back, but experience has shown me that it is extraordinarily unlikely to happen. Hence &quot;dead and gone&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426470#post426470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more deserving is your opinion. it is clearly not an opinion shared by many others here, if you're complaints about how others keep brining up Keychain are anything to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand. By &quot;more deserving&quot; I meant that people are working hard on their own Exalted webcomics that are constantly overlooked because of KoC. I want those comics to be brought up in conversation more, rather than a comic that has been inactive for years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426470#post426470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once more, if &quot;dead and not coming back&quot; meant something wasn't viable inspiration, then you have to toss Gilgamesh, the Greek Heroes, Norse Mythology, most ancient Chinese or Japanese Legends, and a crap ton of classic Anime down the garbage disposal along with Keychain, and then Exalted doesn't exist in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with the current conversation, so beyond this sentence, I'm not going to address it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426470#post426470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have nothing to argue with but opinions, and opinions don't win arguments.<br /> <br /> good day sir.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, which is why I'm arguing using my experiences with other webcomics, not my opinions. Thank you for helping me remember to avoid using opinions in arguments, they tend to creep up without the user realizing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:02:48-08:00","id":426651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426632#post426632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand me. My point is, he can't very well give them as examples of things that are &quot;dead and not coming back&quot; because they are <i>by definition</i> <b>alive and well.</b><br /> <br /> <i>Adaptation is life.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's entirely the point though. The original stories are over, their authors are dead and cannot continue work on them. Yet they persist because people talk about them and build on them. Like KoC (save that the author isn't dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:45:02-08:00","id":426701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426646#post426646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand. By &quot;more deserving&quot; I meant that people are working hard on their own Exalted webcomics that are constantly overlooked because of KoC. I want those comics to be brought up in conversation more, rather than a comic that has been inactive for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want it done right, do it yourself.<br /> I haven't found an Exalted Webcomic that managed to hold my attention (safe for Keychain, which <i>brought me to Exalted</i>), hence, I don't quote anything except KoC, and I have no obligation to do otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:21:46-08:00","id":426722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426701#post426701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want it done right, do it yourself.<br /> I haven't found an Exalted Webcomic that managed to hold my attention (safe for Keychain, which <i>brought me to Exalted</i>), hence, I don't quote anything except KoC, and I have no obligation to do otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are content to cling to a comic that has been inactive for years and is unlikely to ever continue again while other people move on to other things that have the potential to be just as interesting, then by all means, do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:41:21-08:00","id":426755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426722#post426722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are content to cling to a comic that has been inactive for years and is unlikely to ever continue again while other people move on to other things that have the potential to be just as interesting, then by all means, do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would do more good to those webcomics to link to them rather than putting down folks for liking what they like.<br /> That said, I'd be interested in seeing some of those. I only know like 3 that even remotely relate to Exalted (thematically), KoC and Kill Six Billion Demons being two of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:54:20-08:00","id":426763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426755#post426755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would do more good to those webcomics to link to them rather than putting down folks for liking what they like.<br /> That said, I'd be interested in seeing some of those. I only know like 3 that even remotely relate to Exalted (thematically), KoC and Kill Six Billion Demons being two of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will acknowledge the superiority of your argument by providing you with <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com\" target=\"_blank\">God Kicking Boot</a> and <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">Tales of Exalts</a>, both of which can currently be found on the front page of the forums if someone wishes to join in the discussion. There is also a third one by.. Erkon, I believe, which I always forget to save but jump all over once it updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:22:41-08:00","id":426810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426722#post426722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are content to cling to a comic that has been inactive for years and is unlikely to ever continue again while other people move on to other things that have the potential to be just as interesting, then by all means, do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not &quot;clinging&quot; to it. I'm simply reading several other webcomics, KoC is merely the only <i>Exalted</i> webcomic that ever caught my eye, and I'm confident that should it ever resume, there'll be a topic on the front page of this forum talking about it. Otherwise, I'll probably notice it through Comic Rocket, or when I stumble across it again in a few years.<br /> If I see something that relates to things I remember from KoC (or another webcomic, like XKCD, Oglaf, Schlock Mercenary (those were all comics I linked to recently) or any other webcomic I can remember stuff from, for that matter), I post a link.<br /> Since I have never seen another Exalted webcomic that held my attention enough to read a sizable chunk of it, I can't post links to any of them. That's not my problem - they didn't interest me enough to read them, why should I link to them?<br /> But you apparently know several. You know how to give them more attention? <i>Post links</i>. Preferably relevant ones. I have a long list of other stuff to read and link to, I'm not going to do it.<br /> <br /> So, again, this time not hidden behind a common saying:<br /> If you want people to notice other webcomics besides KoC more, you have to <i>link</i> to them. If you can't come up with relevant links to these other comics, then, well... bad luck, I guess. But don't blame KoC for being applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:19:42-08:00","id":426918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426810#post426810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not &quot;clinging&quot; to it. I'm simply reading several other webcomics, KoC is merely the only <i>Exalted</i> webcomic that ever caught my eye, and I'm confident that should it ever resume, there'll be a topic on the front page of this forum talking about it. Otherwise, I'll probably notice it through Comic Rocket, or when I stumble across it again in a few years.<br /> If I see something that relates to things I remember from KoC (or another webcomic, like XKCD, Oglaf, Schlock Mercenary (those were all comics I linked to recently) or any other webcomic I can remember stuff from, for that matter), I post a link.<br /> Since I have never seen another Exalted webcomic that held my attention enough to read a sizable chunk of it, I can't post links to any of them. That's not my problem - they didn't interest me enough to read them, why should I link to them?<br /> But you apparently know several. You know how to give them more attention? <i>Post links</i>. Preferably relevant ones. I have a long list of other stuff to read and link to, I'm not going to do it.<br /> <br /> So, again, this time not hidden behind a common saying:<br /> If you want people to notice other webcomics besides KoC more, you have to <i>link</i> to them. If you can't come up with relevant links to these other comics, then, well... bad luck, I guess. But don't blame KoC for being applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must not have seen my prior post before making this comment, as I did just that. Don't feel bad, though, I do the same thing all the time. The perils of posting on an internet forum, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T15:27:43-08:00","id":427051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/23830-exalted-webcomics-old-and-new\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/23830-exalted-webcomics-old-and-new\"> Exalted Webcomics, Old and New - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/23830-exalted-webcomics-old-and-new\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/23830-exalted-webcomics-old-and-new </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It seems my original idea of a Webcomic database type thingy has expanded, so I'm starting to add particularly notable non-webcomic Exalted media. Actual Webcomics </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Have people never opened the Useful Links thread ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T17:24:46-08:00","id":427134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=426609#post426609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to let Rater202 know, thanks for the tip!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're obviously trying to bait me.<br /> <br /> Though I'll have you know that I argue from <i>informed</i> opinions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunars should actually hunt on the Sacred Hunt because the Sacred hunt is the hunting method of gaining shapes&quot; is an informed opinion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunar charms should be mostly physical rather than magical and glowy because the devs told us that Lunar Powers are physical and visceral and usually involve shapeshifting or otherwise changing themselves or perceptions of themselves&quot; is an informed opinion.<br /> <br /> Informed opinions are valid place to argue from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T18:36:32-08:00","id":427214,"title":"","content":"Subtlety is not appreciated on these forums, I see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T19:02:08-08:00","id":427229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/400234-lunaaaars-this-is-a-lunar-thread?p=427134#post427134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're obviously trying to bait me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have much trust in people, do you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I'll have you know that I argue from <i>informed</i> opinions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunars should actually hunt on the Sacred Hunt because the Sacred hunt is the hunting method of gaining shapes&quot; is an informed opinion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunar charms should be mostly physical rather than magical and glowy because the devs told us that Lunar Powers are physical and visceral and usually involve shapeshifting or otherwise changing themselves or perceptions of themselves&quot; is an informed opinion.<br /> <br /> Informed opinions are valid place to argue from. </div> </div> </div>An informed opinion is still by definition an opinion &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T19:20:59-08:00","id":427238,"title":"","content":"Let me rephrase, because I wasn't clear: An uninformed opinion, or an opinion in which being informed has no relevance, such as a situation where an opinion is purely subjective, is not a valid position to argue from.<br /> <br /> An <i>informed</i> opinion, in a situation where an opinion can be not purely subjective, such as the opinion that &quot;X should be Y and not Z because the Devs said the Devs said that Lunars are X and Y is incompatible with X&quot; is a valid position to argue from, because that opinion is basically &quot;I want them to be aht the Devs said they are&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"ht